1
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:07,704
♫ In the not-too-distant future

2
00:00:07,704 --> 00:00:11,152
♫ Next Sunday A.D.

3
00:00:11,152 --> 00:00:13,926
♫ There was a guy named Joel

4
00:00:13,926 --> 00:00:17,238
♫ Not too different from you or me

5
00:00:17,238 --> 00:00:20,112
♫ He worked at Gizmonic Institute

6
00:00:20,112 --> 00:00:23,460
♫ Just another face in a red jumpsuit

7
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:26,330
♫ He did a good job cleaning up the place

8
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:27,675
♫ But his bosses didn't like him

9
00:00:27,675 --> 00:00:31,508
♫ So they shot him into space

10
00:00:32,774 --> 00:00:36,021
♫ We'll send him cheesy movies

11
00:00:36,021 --> 00:00:38,264
♫ The worst we can find

12
00:00:38,264 --> 00:00:39,097
♫ La la la

13
00:00:39,097 --> 00:00:42,081
♫ He'll have to sit and watch them all

14
00:00:42,081 --> 00:00:44,498
♫ And we'll monitor his mind

15
00:00:44,498 --> 00:00:45,331
♫ La la la

16
00:00:45,331 --> 00:00:48,136
♫ Now keep in mind Joel can't control

17
00:00:48,136 --> 00:00:50,754
♫ When the movies begin or end

18
00:00:50,754 --> 00:00:51,587
♫ La la la

19
00:00:51,587 --> 00:00:54,818
♫ Because he used those special parts

20
00:00:54,818 --> 00:00:58,485
♫ To make his robot friends

21
00:00:59,549 --> 00:01:01,032
♫ Robot Roll Call

22
00:01:01,032 --> 00:01:02,536
♫ Cambot

23
00:01:02,536 --> 00:01:03,844
♫ Gypsy

24
00:01:03,844 --> 00:01:05,656
♫ Tom Servo

25
00:01:05,656 --> 00:01:07,280
♫ Crow

26
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:10,311
♫ If you're wondering
how he eats and breathes

27
00:01:10,311 --> 00:01:12,546
♫ And other science facts

28
00:01:12,546 --> 00:01:13,379
♫ La la la

29
00:01:13,379 --> 00:01:16,278
♫ Then repeat to yourself it's just a show

30
00:01:16,278 --> 00:01:19,405
♫ I should really just relax

31
00:01:19,405 --> 00:01:21,185
♫ For Mystery Science

32
00:01:21,185 --> 00:01:25,352
♫ Theater 3000 ♫

33
00:01:26,509 --> 00:01:29,259
(doors slamming)

34
00:01:34,502 --> 00:01:35,889
- Oh!

35
00:01:35,889 --> 00:01:38,513
Got five seconds to live!

36
00:01:38,513 --> 00:01:42,706
Must get personal finances in order.

37
00:01:42,706 --> 00:01:43,761
- [Crow] Joel, Joel!

38
00:01:43,761 --> 00:01:44,881
Thank heavens you made it!

39
00:01:44,881 --> 00:01:46,316
What the heck was that thing?

40
00:01:46,316 --> 00:01:47,617
We lost Tom, buddy!

41
00:01:47,617 --> 00:01:49,910
I hate to think of him in there with that,

42
00:01:49,910 --> 00:01:51,894
that, wait a minute, I'm blind!

43
00:01:51,894 --> 00:01:54,444
I'm blind, that thing cut me!

44
00:01:54,444 --> 00:01:58,951
- [Tom] Crow, something
is wrong on Saturn Three.

45
00:01:58,951 --> 00:02:00,301
Crow buddy, Crow!

46
00:02:00,301 --> 00:02:01,773
- [Crow] It looks like I got it man,

47
00:02:01,773 --> 00:02:03,235
at least I found Joel!

48
00:02:03,235 --> 00:02:06,241
The little Pantyweight passed
out in all the excitement!

49
00:02:06,241 --> 00:02:08,323
- [Tom] Keep telling yourself that, Crow!

50
00:02:08,323 --> 00:02:09,760
(sobbing)

51
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:11,547
- [Crow] What do you
mean, Tom, you're crying!

52
00:02:11,547 --> 00:02:12,380
What?

53
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:14,390
We're all together again!
- [Tom] Crow!

54
00:02:14,390 --> 00:02:16,723
(crosstalk)

55
00:02:18,633 --> 00:02:21,046
Joel Robinson is dead!

56
00:02:21,046 --> 00:02:23,535
- [Crow] Oh god, he's dead!

57
00:02:23,535 --> 00:02:24,720
- [All] Face.

58
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:25,857
- Just kiddin'.

59
00:02:25,857 --> 00:02:27,247
- [Crow] Hey, you look great.

60
00:02:27,247 --> 00:02:29,830
(upbeat music)

61
00:02:33,029 --> 00:02:34,458
(laughing)

62
00:02:34,458 --> 00:02:36,793
- Oh, we do have fun, don't we?

63
00:02:36,793 --> 00:02:37,626
- Yes.

64
00:02:37,626 --> 00:02:39,002
- What was that line again, Crow?

65
00:02:39,002 --> 00:02:41,614
- Oh, you mean, "I'm
blind, that thing cut me!"

66
00:02:41,614 --> 00:02:44,378
- No no no, that other one, "Don't you--"

67
00:02:44,378 --> 00:02:46,489
- Oh yeah, oh yeah, "Don't you do it!"

68
00:02:46,489 --> 00:02:48,041
(laughing)

69
00:02:48,041 --> 00:02:50,043
Just a second, the Mads are calling.

70
00:02:50,043 --> 00:02:51,539
- Don't you ever let me catch you

71
00:02:51,539 --> 00:02:52,945
fooling around like that up there.

72
00:02:52,945 --> 00:02:54,056
Well if I was up there right now,

73
00:02:54,056 --> 00:02:55,582
I'd spank your hinder.

74
00:02:55,582 --> 00:02:56,670
- Well let's just rage on with

75
00:02:56,670 --> 00:02:58,264
the invention exchange, Frank.

76
00:02:58,264 --> 00:03:00,238
Tall and proud.

77
00:03:00,238 --> 00:03:01,603
- Okay.

78
00:03:01,603 --> 00:03:03,191
My name is Bond,

79
00:03:03,191 --> 00:03:04,174
Frank Bond.

80
00:03:04,174 --> 00:03:06,360
- Right and I'm Ursula Andress.

81
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:07,586
- I know.

82
00:03:07,586 --> 00:03:10,563
- Do I have to do everything
around here, Frank?

83
00:03:10,563 --> 00:03:12,344
- Oh sorry boss, it's
just that when you're

84
00:03:12,344 --> 00:03:14,680
a top secret agent with a license to kill,

85
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:17,432
like myself, you always
find yourself in SCUBA gear.

86
00:03:17,432 --> 00:03:19,715
But not only that, there's
that endless series of

87
00:03:19,715 --> 00:03:23,480
formal parties, dances and
dinners that you have to attend.

88
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:27,052
I mean, it's really easy to
fit a tuxedo under a wetsuit,

89
00:03:27,052 --> 00:03:28,494
but what about footwear?

90
00:03:28,494 --> 00:03:29,975
- Show the product, Frank.

91
00:03:29,975 --> 00:03:31,640
Smile.

92
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:33,411
Introducing the formal flippers,

93
00:03:33,411 --> 00:03:34,889
step out of the ocean and into

94
00:03:34,889 --> 00:03:37,662
high society with the formal flipper.

95
00:03:37,662 --> 00:03:38,590
- By Bass.

96
00:03:38,590 --> 00:03:40,008
And what about the Ladies?

97
00:03:40,008 --> 00:03:41,429
- The ladies?

98
00:03:41,429 --> 00:03:42,679
Pan down Jerry.

99
00:03:44,526 --> 00:03:47,393
- [Frank] Hello, Federov.

100
00:03:47,393 --> 00:03:49,859
- Oh, could we just get on
with your invention exchange,

101
00:03:49,859 --> 00:03:52,222
you blinking pinkie ring?

102
00:03:52,222 --> 00:03:53,722
- I want children.

103
00:03:55,533 --> 00:03:58,018
- You know Joel, every day, in every way,

104
00:03:58,018 --> 00:04:00,130
those guys are gettin'
weirder and weirder.

105
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:01,741
- I know, I couldn't
agree more with you more.

106
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:04,130
Anyway, my invention exchange today

107
00:04:04,130 --> 00:04:05,613
is based on the premise

108
00:04:05,613 --> 00:04:08,525
that kids just don't like to
wear hats in the winter time.

109
00:04:08,525 --> 00:04:11,233
You know, I mean hats mat your hair down.

110
00:04:11,233 --> 00:04:13,773
Headbands make your hair all static-y

111
00:04:13,773 --> 00:04:16,023
and earmuffs just plain look dorky.

112
00:04:16,023 --> 00:04:17,602
- You know I remember winter,

113
00:04:17,602 --> 00:04:19,786
sleddin' down the back
hill, over the creek,

114
00:04:19,786 --> 00:04:22,850
under the old bridge, past the
Sullivan's big dog, Trouser.

115
00:04:22,850 --> 00:04:24,354
Wavin' to Lois and Sabrina--

116
00:04:24,354 --> 00:04:25,922
- Yeah yeah, whatever!

117
00:04:25,922 --> 00:04:27,895
- Anyway, anyway you two.

118
00:04:27,895 --> 00:04:30,187
This is a new invention that will

119
00:04:30,187 --> 00:04:33,058
allow kids to look cool and stay warm

120
00:04:33,058 --> 00:04:36,226
and avoid all that peer
mockery that we all know

121
00:04:36,226 --> 00:04:38,477
can harm us well into adulthood.

122
00:04:38,477 --> 00:04:39,693
Check it out!

123
00:04:39,693 --> 00:04:42,189
They're earmuffs that look like ears!

124
00:04:42,189 --> 00:04:43,022
See what I mean?

125
00:04:43,022 --> 00:04:46,183
Okay, put them on,
let's see how they look.

126
00:04:46,183 --> 00:04:47,099
Okay.

127
00:04:47,099 --> 00:04:49,360
- Hey, I feel like Prince Charles.

128
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:51,953
- Yeah, and they'll come
in a rainbow of colors,

129
00:04:51,953 --> 00:04:55,110
eventually, to match
everybody's countenance.

130
00:04:55,110 --> 00:04:56,305
Okay, look.

131
00:04:56,305 --> 00:04:59,473
- Oh, so suddenly I look
like Jimmie JJ Walker.

132
00:04:59,473 --> 00:05:01,414
- Right, and they'll also come

133
00:05:01,414 --> 00:05:03,550
in a lot of novelty styles too.

134
00:05:03,550 --> 00:05:06,932
Like for next year's big sci-fi levia-thon

135
00:05:06,932 --> 00:05:09,313
in Anchorage, Alaska, I've invented

136
00:05:09,313 --> 00:05:11,146
these Vulcan earmuffs.

137
00:05:12,532 --> 00:05:14,113
See?

138
00:05:14,113 --> 00:05:15,401
- Fascinating.

139
00:05:15,401 --> 00:05:17,249
Live long and prosper.

140
00:05:17,249 --> 00:05:18,082
Not!

141
00:05:18,082 --> 00:05:19,329
(laughing)

142
00:05:19,329 --> 00:05:21,249
- Also, Joel, we don't see you wearing

143
00:05:21,249 --> 00:05:23,083
any of these dopey earmuffs.

144
00:05:23,083 --> 00:05:24,043
- Yeah, what's the deal?

145
00:05:24,043 --> 00:05:25,257
- Oh, well you guys,

146
00:05:25,257 --> 00:05:26,827
looks are deceiving.

147
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:31,189
You see, not only am I
president of Ear Club For Men,

148
00:05:31,189 --> 00:05:32,856
I'm also a customer.

149
00:05:33,746 --> 00:05:35,093
What do you think, sirs?

150
00:05:35,093 --> 00:05:37,003
- Very nice Sy Sperling.

151
00:05:37,003 --> 00:05:39,382
Tell 'em about the
experiment this week, Frank.

152
00:05:39,382 --> 00:05:41,899
- This week's experiment is called Jack,

153
00:05:41,899 --> 00:05:43,275
Mighty Jack.

154
00:05:43,275 --> 00:05:45,078
It's produced by Frank,

155
00:05:45,078 --> 00:05:46,892
Sandy Frank.

156
00:05:46,892 --> 00:05:48,531
- Push the button, send
'em the movie, Frank,

157
00:05:48,531 --> 00:05:50,803
I gotta get outta these size nines.

158
00:05:50,803 --> 00:05:52,989
(buzzing)
- [All] What, huh?

159
00:05:52,989 --> 00:05:53,822
What?

160
00:05:53,822 --> 00:05:56,390
- We've got movies on!

161
00:05:56,390 --> 00:05:59,057
(doors opening)

162
00:06:04,386 --> 00:06:06,699
- [Joel] Those guys are...
- [Tom] Great legs though.

163
00:06:06,699 --> 00:06:07,947
Hey, Mighty Jack!

164
00:06:07,947 --> 00:06:09,440
The story of a brave pancake.

165
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:11,616
Starring Aunt Jemima
and Flap the wonder dog!

166
00:06:11,616 --> 00:06:14,132
- [Joel] Mighty Jack, the
dog, isn't that a dog food?

167
00:06:14,132 --> 00:06:16,297
- [Tom] Could be.

168
00:06:16,297 --> 00:06:19,339
Featuring our all-vegetarian dishes!

169
00:06:19,339 --> 00:06:22,683
Hitaki Teriyaki and Nakayo Koko.

170
00:06:22,683 --> 00:06:26,121
- [Crow] They should really
waterproof this basement.

171
00:06:26,121 --> 00:06:27,422
- [Tom] George!

172
00:06:27,422 --> 00:06:28,777
Marcia!

173
00:06:28,777 --> 00:06:30,855
Corn job!
- [Crow] Huh?

174
00:06:30,855 --> 00:06:33,241
- [Tom] Kinda soap opera music here.

175
00:06:33,241 --> 00:06:36,505
♫ I am a lineman for the Starfleet

176
00:06:36,505 --> 00:06:39,460
♫ Yee hoo ♫

177
00:06:39,460 --> 00:06:40,996
- [Crow] Lovebird 2000,

178
00:06:40,996 --> 00:06:43,128
