Q Note Cafe, the Q-Tips.

233
00:08:45,409 --> 00:08:48,108
(jazzy music)

234
00:08:48,108 --> 00:08:50,134
- [Voiceover] Tokyo, 10 AM.

235
00:08:50,134 --> 00:08:52,534
- [Crow] Do you know
where your children are?

236
00:08:52,534 --> 00:08:54,345
- [Voiceover] Saigon, 7:30 AM.

237
00:08:54,345 --> 00:08:58,048
- [Joel] Hey, he's eating Q rations.

238
00:08:58,048 --> 00:09:00,733
- [Voiceover] Moscow, 7:00 AM.

239
00:09:00,733 --> 00:09:02,471
And Paris, 2:00 AM.

240
00:09:02,471 --> 00:09:05,026
- [Joel] Ah, Paris, city of lamps.

241
00:09:05,026 --> 00:09:07,693
- [Crow] Hey look, Richard
Carpenter's gettin' drunk!

242
00:09:07,693 --> 00:09:09,962
- [Joel] Unbelievable, and Karen.

243
00:09:09,962 --> 00:09:11,143
Come on, finish it!

244
00:09:11,143 --> 00:09:12,530
- [Crow] Finish it, woo!

245
00:09:12,530 --> 00:09:15,113
- [Tom] Hey, Geraldine Ferraro!

246
00:09:17,355 --> 00:09:19,962
- [Joel] Who's the guy?
- [Crow] Girl.

247
00:09:19,962 --> 00:09:21,905
- [Joel] Hey, it's JFK!

248
00:09:21,905 --> 00:09:22,988
- [Crow] Wow.

249
00:09:23,824 --> 00:09:24,991
- [Tom] Bobby!

250
00:09:27,558 --> 00:09:28,796
- [Crow] Okay, let's see now,

251
00:09:28,796 --> 00:09:30,492
why do bees suddenly reappear?

252
00:09:30,492 --> 00:09:32,492
Oh, screw it, forget it.

253
00:09:33,905 --> 00:09:34,822
- Monsieur.

254
00:09:36,151 --> 00:09:38,027
Won't you stay with me a few more minutes?

255
00:09:38,027 --> 00:09:40,860
- [Crow] While I spackle my teeth.

256
00:09:43,231 --> 00:09:44,577
- [Tom] Hey, Django Reinhardt.

257
00:09:44,577 --> 00:09:45,569
- [Crow] Nah, too many fingers.

258
00:09:45,569 --> 00:09:48,235
- [Tom] Ah, you're right.

259
00:09:48,235 --> 00:09:49,793
- [Crow] A Japanese in Paris!

260
00:09:49,793 --> 00:09:53,126
(mock Japanese singing)

261
00:09:54,470 --> 00:09:55,675
- [Joel] Is that kinda racist?

262
00:09:55,675 --> 00:09:58,649
- [Tom] No, no, I don't think so.

263
00:09:58,649 --> 00:10:01,655
- [Crow] Door is ajar.
- [Tom] Ding dong.

264
00:10:01,655 --> 00:10:03,723
- [Crow] Ignite cigarette.
- [Tom] Ding dong.

265
00:10:03,723 --> 00:10:05,801
- [Crow] Have second
thoughts about girl in bar.

266
00:10:05,801 --> 00:10:07,301
- [Tom] Ding dong.

267
00:10:15,157 --> 00:10:18,251
Oh lord, won't you buy me a Mercedes Benz?

268
00:10:18,251 --> 00:10:20,810
My friends all drive Porsches.

269
00:10:20,810 --> 00:10:25,132
- [Crow] Ah, we're coming
to the fork in the plot!

270
00:10:25,132 --> 00:10:26,656
- [Tom] Don't take a wrong turn.

271
00:10:26,656 --> 00:10:27,498
- [Joel] What?

272
00:10:27,498 --> 00:10:29,310
- [Tom] It's kind of a
Keith Haring painting.

273
00:10:29,310 --> 00:10:32,062
- [Joel] That looks like the...

274
00:10:32,062 --> 00:10:33,929
- [Traffic guard] Halt!

275
00:10:33,929 --> 00:10:35,331
(Crow speaking German)

276
00:10:35,331 --> 00:10:37,916
- [Tom] Shh, Ixnay, French!

277
00:10:37,916 --> 00:10:41,583
- [Crow] Oh, hello monsieur.
- [Tom] Bonjour.

278
00:10:43,396 --> 00:10:44,229
- [Crow] Oh, big one.

279
00:10:44,229 --> 00:10:45,897
- [Joel] Shield your eyes from the net!

280
00:10:45,897 --> 00:10:47,647
- [Tom] Oh, big, big!

281
00:10:50,155 --> 00:10:52,326
- [Joel] It's the helicopter from Daktari!

282
00:10:52,326 --> 00:10:53,509
- [Crow] Oh, they're gonna return

283
00:10:53,509 --> 00:10:56,144
that Japanese car to the wild!

284
00:10:56,144 --> 00:10:58,067
- [Joel] They gotta tag it.

285
00:10:58,067 --> 00:10:59,101
- Bon voyage!

286
00:10:59,101 --> 00:11:02,018
- [Tom] You will always have Paris!

287
00:11:03,784 --> 00:11:05,416
- [Crow] Oh boy.
(car honking)

288
00:11:05,416 --> 00:11:06,406
- [Tom] You know you can always tell

289
00:11:06,406 --> 00:11:08,563
it's a Japanese net, it's
filled with dolphins!

290
00:11:08,563 --> 00:11:09,672
(groaning)

291
00:11:09,672 --> 00:11:10,531
- [Joel] What a burn.

292
00:11:10,531 --> 00:11:13,432
- [Voiceover] Just relax Mr.
Atari and enjoy the ride,

293
00:11:13,432 --> 00:11:14,679
it's a beautiful night--

294
00:11:14,679 --> 00:11:15,980
- [Joel] For a moon dance.

295
00:11:15,980 --> 00:11:18,979
- Look, what do you think you're doing?

296
00:11:18,979 --> 00:11:22,819
- [Voiceover] Your altitude is 2,000 feet.

297
00:11:22,819 --> 00:11:25,923
I'm sure you'll enjoy
the view, good night.

298
00:11:25,923 --> 00:11:29,891
- [Tom] To your left you'll
see the (speaking French).

299
00:11:29,891 --> 00:11:33,558
- [Crow] This is no
place for a convertible!

300
00:11:35,629 --> 00:11:37,546
John Wayne is Branigan!

301
00:11:39,373 --> 00:11:42,060
- [Tom] Medical Center, in color.

302
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:44,391
- [Joel] Ooh, that's good weed!

303
00:11:44,391 --> 00:11:46,054
(laughing)

304
00:11:46,054 --> 00:11:47,634
- [Crow] Hey, it's J. Edgar Hoover.

305
00:11:47,634 --> 00:11:49,404
I will crush the Kennedys.

306
00:11:49,404 --> 00:11:50,237
- Come in.

307
00:11:54,663 --> 00:11:57,084
- It's regarding Mr. Atari.
(slurping)

308
00:11:57,084 --> 00:11:58,802
I made several calls to Paris to try

309
00:11:58,802 --> 00:12:01,766
to get more detailed information.

310
00:12:01,766 --> 00:12:05,170
On the day he disappeared,
Mr. Atari left the cabaret

311
00:12:05,170 --> 00:12:06,631
at two in the morning.

312
00:12:06,631 --> 00:12:09,289
Drove past the--
(sighing)

313
00:12:09,289 --> 00:12:10,678
And then he suddenly disappeared

314
00:12:10,678 --> 00:12:12,277
along the highway somewhere.

315
00:12:12,277 --> 00:12:14,513
- And the airports?

316
00:12:14,513 --> 00:12:15,631
- Nothing as yet.

317
00:12:15,631 --> 00:12:18,464
(sniffing loudly)

318
00:12:22,118 --> 00:12:23,497
(spitting)

319
00:12:23,497 --> 00:12:26,054
- All right, that'll be all, thank you.

320
00:12:26,054 --> 00:12:27,387
- [Joel] Oh god.

321
00:12:30,008 --> 00:12:31,789
I am so high!

322
00:12:31,789 --> 00:12:34,990
- [Voiceover] Not a case of robbery.

323
00:12:34,990 --> 00:12:36,983
I better contact Mighty Jack.

324
00:12:36,983 --> 00:12:38,070
- [Tom] Why is my internal voice

325
00:12:38,070 --> 00:12:40,063
different from my external voice?

326
00:12:40,063 --> 00:12:41,644
Inside, I'm tan and handsome.

327
00:12:41,644 --> 00:12:45,311
Outside, I'm the Grinch
who stole Christmas.

328
00:12:48,074 --> 00:12:49,863
(kisses)

329
00:12:49,863 --> 00:12:52,230
- [Crow] Hello?
- [Joel] Hey.

330
00:12:52,230 --> 00:12:55,431
- Hello, is that you Katherine?

331
00:12:55,431 --> 00:12:59,348
- [Crow] Hey, what are
they opening a boutique?

332
00:13:01,543 --> 00:13:03,430
- [Tom] She'll not have my apple.

333
00:13:03,430 --> 00:13:04,263
It's mine.

334
00:13:06,118 --> 00:13:07,867
- Here's the message from Colonel Yabuki.

335
00:13:07,867 --> 00:13:09,264
- [Joel] My Bookie?

336
00:13:09,264 --> 00:13:11,783
- [Colonel] I want you
to rescue a certain man.

337
00:13:11,783 --> 00:13:13,871
He disappeared suddenly near Paris.

338
00:13:13,871 --> 00:13:15,706
He's very important to Mighty Jack,

339
00:13:15,706 --> 00:13:17,543
it could be a dangerous mission.

340
00:13:17,543 --> 00:13:18,961
So be careful.

341
00:13:18,961 --> 00:13:21,121
- [Joel] Oh, and Sabrina,
you pose as a scientist

342
00:13:21,121 --> 00:13:24,279
and wear that string bikini we got you.

343
00:13:24,279 --> 00:13:25,215
- [Katherine] That's the man.

344
00:13:25,215 --> 00:13:27,692
- [Tom] Say.
- [Crow] That's a man?

345
00:13:27,692 --> 00:13:29,650
- How interesting.

346
00:13:29,650 --> 00:13:31,535
- You know a lot of
girls who look like that?

347
00:13:31,535 --> 00:13:32,527
- This one I do.

348
00:13:32,527 --> 00:13:34,995
She's a well-known dancer.

349
00:13:34,995 --> 00:13:38,106
- She's not missing, it's
the man we're looking for.

350
00:13:38,106 --> 00:13:39,545
- [Crow] Oh, too bad.

351
00:13:39,545 --> 00:13:42,441
- [Jerry] So he's our next assignment.

352
00:13:42,441 --> 00:13:43,657
- [Joel] Measure it.

353
00:13:43,657 --> 00:13:45,081
- [Katherine] His name is Harold Atari.

354
00:13:45,081 --> 00:13:47,987
He's a professional mountaineer.

355
00:13:47,987 --> 00:13:50,570
(upbeat music)

356
00:13:53,737 --> 00:13:55,038
- What about that transmitter?

357
00:13:55,038 --> 00:13:57,545
- [Tom] It kinda looks like
the $10,000 Pyramid here.

358
00:13:57,545 --> 00:13:58,973
- What's being done to find it?

359
00:13:58,973 --> 00:14:00,617
- Captain Tenda and Lieutenant Jerry

360
00:14:00,617 --> 00:14:02,686
are out searching with the electroscout.

361
00:14:02,686 --> 00:14:04,397
- [Joel] Things you see in a Dali shot.

362
00:14:04,397 --> 00:14:07,709
- Well the maximum range is 700 miles.

363
00:14:07,709 --> 00:14:09,786
- [Crow] Things you'd say to Marconi.

364
00:14:09,786 --> 00:14:10,894
- If it's within that radius--

365
00:14:10,894 --> 00:14:13,371
- [Tom] Things you keep in your purse!

366
00:14:13,371 --> 00:14:14,630
- There's one slight problem though--

367
00:14:14,630 --> 00:14:15,952
- [Joel] Things you say when you're dead!

368
00:14:15,952 --> 00:14:19,088
- Mr. Atari doesn't know he
has the transmitter on him.

369
00:14:19,088 --> 00:14:20,720
- Then he won't know that we...

370
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:23,983
- You see Katherine, I had it
issued merely as a precaution.

371
00:14:23,983 --> 00:14:25,061
- [Tom] Things you say in a T top.

372
00:14:25,061 --> 00:14:28,168
- Mr. Atari was called away very suddenly,

373
00:14:28,168 --> 00:14:31,363
before he was instructed in its uses.

374
00:14:31,363 --> 00:14:33,048
- If he doesn't find it then...

375
00:14:33,048 --> 00:14:34,305
- Sooner or later--

376
00:14:34,305 --> 00:14:37,389
- [Tom] Love is going to get you.

377
00:14:37,389 --> 00:14:38,892
- Bless us, our Buddha,

378
00:14:38,892 --> 00:14:40,328
wait, I'm not a Buddhist.

379
00:14:40,328 --> 00:14:42,797
- [Tom] He's a Shinto.

380
00:14:42,797 --> 00:14:43,964
Wait a minute!

381
00:14:44,856 --> 00:14:48,568
Button, button, I've got the button!

382
00:14:48,568 --> 00:14:50,318
I'm gonna use it too.

383
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:54,620
- [Joel] Hmm, it's kinda dull.

384
00:14:56,207 --> 00:14:57,447
- [Tom] Like this movie?

385
00:14:57,447 --> 00:14:59,697
(laughing)

386
00:15:02,792 --> 00:15:04,467
(explosion)
- [Crow] Huzzah, alakazam!

387
00:15:04,467 --> 00:15:05,629
And I'm gone!

388
00:15:05,629 --> 00:15:07,661
Oh, I gotta work on that.

389
00:15:07,661 --> 00:15:09,379
Got the patter down though.

390
00:15:09,379 --> 00:15:10,431
- [Joel] If I'm not mistaken,

391
00:15:10,431 --> 00:15:13,731
I should have a rabbit
over there, at least.

392
00:15:13,731 --> 00:15:15,203
Huh?

393
00:15:15,203 --> 00:15:18,123
(gasping)

394
00:15:18,123 --> 00:15:20,706
Oh, I was just daydreaming, Dr.

395
00:15:23,047 --> 00:15:25,565
- Very well, and when are you coming back?

396
00:15:25,565 --> 00:15:27,176
- I'm not sure.

397
00:15:27,176 --> 00:15:29,352
- Don't stay away too long.

398
00:15:29,352 --> 00:15:31,219
- [Crow] If you know what I mean.

399
00:15:31,219 --> 00:15:32,052
(laughing)

400
00:15:32,052 --> 00:15:34,642
- You've always been one of our best men.

401
00:15:34,642 --> 00:15:36,275
- Thank you sir.
- [Crow] I think.

402
00:15:36,275 --> 00:15:38,696
- Oh, do you see that box there?

403
00:15:38,696 --> 00:15:41,331
That suit, it's my parting gift to you.

404
00:15:41,331 --> 00:15:44,471
- [Tom] From Spiegal,
Chicago, Illinois, 60609.

405
00:15:44,471 --> 00:15:46,355
- [Joel] Wait a minute,
is this a flashback?

406
00:15:46,355 --> 00:15:47,855
- [Crow] I'm lost.

407
00:15:50,995 --> 00:15:54,355
Hmm, good workmanship,
Morty must've made this.

408
00:15:54,355 --> 00:15:55,592
- [Tom] Nice Hanky poof too.

409
00:15:55,592 --> 00:15:57,117
- [Joel] Hmm, what a weird guy,

410
00:15:57,117 --> 00:16:01,284
gives lovely parting gifts
after a meeting, but I...

411
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,373
- Hear anything?

412
00:16:05,373 --> 00:16:07,944
- [Crow] No, I've got
wood clamps on my ears!

413
00:16:07,944 --> 00:16:11,818
- It's no use, I'm not getting a signal.

414
00:16:11,818 --> 00:16:13,571
- I'm gonna try further west.

415
00:16:13,571 --> 00:16:15,488
- [Tom] Crest, Crest...

416
00:16:17,453 --> 00:16:18,557
(farting noise)

417
00:16:18,557 --> 00:16:21,430
- [Tom] Ha ha, I love that one.

418
00:16:21,430 --> 00:16:24,406
- [Crow] Hi boys and girls,
I'm gonna take my shoes off

419
00:16:24,406 --> 00:16:27,104
and put my little sneakers on.

420
00:16:27,104 --> 00:16:28,606
(sniffs)
(groaning)

421
00:16:28,606 --> 00:16:30,405
- [Joel] Oh man, you need Dr. Scholls!

422
00:16:30,405 --> 00:16:34,719
It either smells like
bad meat or good cheese!

423
00:16:34,719 --> 00:16:36,506
- [Tom] If I'm not
mistaken there's a phone...

424
00:16:36,506 --> 00:16:38,923
Oh no, that's just my insole.

425
00:16:40,037 --> 00:16:41,956
- [Joel] Oh I see, there's a he...

426
00:16:41,956 --> 00:16:43,269
A really good he...

427
00:16:43,269 --> 00:16:44,102
What?

428
00:16:46,091 --> 00:16:47,318
- [Tom] Cherry cordials?

429
00:16:47,318 --> 00:16:49,485
What a thoughtful old man!

430
00:16:55,299 --> 00:16:58,661
- [Crow] Playin' house is
fun, table for two sir?

431
00:16:58,661 --> 00:16:59,763
Oui,

432
00:16:59,763 --> 00:17:00,766
oui.

433
00:17:00,766 --> 00:17:04,516
I'm havin' a tea party
for my little friends.

434
00:17:05,897 --> 00:17:07,017
Coat's a real rip off!

435
00:17:07,017 --> 00:17:08,905
Wouldn't ya say...

436
00:17:08,905 --> 00:17:10,439
- [Tom] Let's see, paperclip,

437
00:17:10,439 --> 00:17:14,963
an old stick of gum, see
what else I got in here.

438
00:17:14,963 --> 00:17:16,531
Oh, a bunch of peanut shells from that

439
00:17:16,531 --> 00:17:18,579
karaoke bar stuck in there.

440
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:19,625
For cryin' out loud.

441
00:17:19,625 --> 00:17:20,990
- [Joel] Well, he's building a meal.

442
00:17:20,990 --> 00:17:22,771
You see he's got the
four button groups there.

443
00:17:22,771 --> 00:17:24,604
- [Tom] Oh, of course.

444
00:17:26,705 --> 00:17:29,303
(humming)

445
00:17:29,303 --> 00:17:30,723
- [Crow] I did it one piece at a time

446
00:17:30,723 --> 00:17:33,140
and it didn't cost me a dime!

447
00:17:34,446 --> 00:17:38,111
Ah great, the instructions
are in Japanese.

448
00:17:38,111 --> 00:17:40,611
(tom humming)

449
00:17:45,219 --> 00:17:46,846
(chuckling)
- [Joel] It's a one-hitter.

450
00:17:46,846 --> 00:17:49,096
(laughing)

451
00:17:50,878 --> 00:17:53,118
- [Tom] What's he doing there?

452
00:17:53,118 --> 00:17:56,776
That really held his
tie in place, didn't it?

453
00:17:56,776 --> 00:17:58,034
- [Crow] Maybe he can get into the

454
00:17:58,034 --> 00:17:59,443
craft fair next year with that.

455
00:17:59,443 --> 00:18:00,883
(electronic buzzing)

456
00:18:00,883 --> 00:18:01,883
- [All] Hmm?

457
00:18:03,134 --> 00:18:04,604
- [Atari] They might be monitoring it.

458
00:18:04,604 --> 00:18:06,342
- [Joel] They might be giants.

459
00:18:06,342 --> 00:18:09,843
(electronic buzzing)
- [Tom] There it is again.

460
00:18:09,843 --> 00:18:11,006
- [Joel] This is only a test.

461
00:18:11,006 --> 00:18:13,673
Had this been an actual movie...

462
00:18:14,771 --> 00:18:16,818
- It's gone again.

463
00:18:16,818 --> 00:18:18,227
- There's one thing pretty sure though,

464
00:18:18,227 --> 00:18:19,795
that was on the 20 meter band.

465
00:18:19,795 --> 00:18:21,688
- [Joel] Bootsy's 20 meter band?

466
00:18:21,688 --> 00:18:24,334
- It's much too far to figure out sir.

467
00:18:24,334 --> 00:18:27,251
- Try to get the general direction.

468
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,752
- [Tom] Uh, that way?
- Pacific Ocean!

469
00:18:29,752 --> 00:18:31,128
- [Crow] A specific ocean?

470
00:18:31,128 --> 00:18:33,101
Yeah, but which one, be more Pacific!

471
00:18:33,101 --> 00:18:35,048
(laughing)

472
00:18:35,048 --> 00:18:36,752
- Jerry, look!
- [Tom] Jerry?

473
00:18:36,752 --> 00:18:40,498
- [Crow] Dean, we're flying
in the thing with the hole!

474
00:18:40,498 --> 00:18:41,665
- [Tom] Crest.

475
00:18:42,961 --> 00:18:43,794
Oh look.

476
00:18:44,732 --> 00:18:46,748
It must be a wedding,
they're throwing rice.

477
00:18:46,748 --> 00:18:48,721
Really big rice.

478
00:18:48,721 --> 00:18:52,956
- [Joel] They're holding
hands and skimming stones.

479
00:18:52,956 --> 00:18:56,623
- [Tom] Toy boat.
- [All] Toy boat, toy boat.

480
00:18:57,711 --> 00:19:00,744
- [Tom] Oh, it's the
captain of the Valdez there.

481
00:19:00,744 --> 00:19:02,211
- [Crow] Stately plump Buck Mulligan

482
00:19:02,211 --> 00:19:03,543
came down from the stairwell...

483
00:19:03,543 --> 00:19:05,293
This book is awful.

484
00:19:05,293 --> 00:19:07,042
Hmm, no pictures.

485
00:19:07,042 --> 00:19:07,875
- Doctor.

486
00:19:08,750 --> 00:19:11,024
I've got this awful headache.

487
00:19:11,024 --> 00:19:12,053
- [Tom] Okay, climb in.

488
00:19:12,053 --> 00:19:13,194
- Looks like you're homesick again.

489
00:19:13,194 --> 00:19:16,108
- Oh no, it's not that at all.

490
00:19:16,108 --> 00:19:17,706
It's those crazy radio signals,

491
00:19:17,706 --> 00:19:20,691
they get louder and softer
and softer and louder.

492
00:19:20,691 --> 00:19:23,043
They're driving me out of my mind!

493
00:19:23,043 --> 00:19:25,269
But I'm getting a lot of interference.

494
00:19:25,269 --> 00:19:28,170
They're transmitting
about every 10 minutes.

495
00:19:28,170 --> 00:19:32,447
(sniffs)
- [Joel] Butyl nitrate?

496
00:19:32,447 --> 00:19:33,631
- Something suspicious though,

497
00:19:33,631 --> 00:19:35,967
there's no station on the 20 meter band.

498
00:19:35,967 --> 00:19:37,802
- [Crow] It's a calamity!

499
00:19:37,802 --> 00:19:39,690
- You say it's on the 20 meter band?

500
00:19:39,690 --> 00:19:41,365
- [Crow] Yes.

501
00:19:41,365 --> 00:19:43,935
- Maybe that's Atari.

502
00:19:43,935 --> 00:19:46,015
Try to get the exact
direction of those signals.

503
00:19:46,015 --> 00:19:47,242
Do it immediately!

504
00:19:47,242 --> 00:19:49,428
- Couldn't you give me some
medicine first, Doctor?

505
00:19:49,428 --> 00:19:52,618
- [Tom] I'd prescribe
me, Dr. Chad Feelgood.

506
00:19:52,618 --> 00:19:55,743
Meanwhile, back on the Greasy Bastard...

507
00:19:55,743 --> 00:19:56,991
- When did you start hearing them?

508
00:19:56,991 --> 00:19:58,293
- [Crow] When I was 10.

509
00:19:58,293 --> 00:20:01,205
- I picked up the first
signals a few days ago.

510
00:20:01,205 --> 00:20:04,362
I was trying to get headquarters,
but reception was bad,

511
00:20:04,362 --> 00:20:07,893
so I changed wavebands and noticed it.

512
00:20:07,893 --> 00:20:11,647
