00:29:41,347 --> 00:29:42,893
Unless you're all frightened pigeons!

763
00:29:42,893 --> 00:29:44,535
- Boy, that's the last straw!

764
00:29:44,535 --> 00:29:45,453
Pigeon yourself!

765
00:29:45,453 --> 00:29:46,584
- [Crow] Hey, watch your mouth!

766
00:29:46,584 --> 00:29:47,981
- [Atari] If you don't think
you can handle the job,

767
00:29:47,981 --> 00:29:49,857
you might as well turn around and go home.

768
00:29:49,857 --> 00:29:51,789
- [Tom] Ooh, what a burn!

769
00:29:51,789 --> 00:29:53,336
- Well I've had enough!

770
00:29:53,336 --> 00:29:54,872
All right, let's go home!

771
00:29:54,872 --> 00:29:56,312
Why should we save him?

772
00:29:56,312 --> 00:29:59,587
- [Joel] Look, heckling
is part of the business.

773
00:29:59,587 --> 00:30:01,452
- I admire his courage.

774
00:30:01,452 --> 00:30:03,160
- [Crow] You would, kiss up.

775
00:30:03,160 --> 00:30:04,717
- [Voiceover] Do you read me, Mighty Jack?

776
00:30:04,717 --> 00:30:07,050
Well, what have you decided?

777
00:30:08,686 --> 00:30:09,944
- We read you all right.

778
00:30:09,944 --> 00:30:11,971
We need a little time.

779
00:30:11,971 --> 00:30:12,963
- [Voiceover] Very well.

780
00:30:12,963 --> 00:30:15,181
We'll take this up with Colonel Yabuki.

781
00:30:15,181 --> 00:30:18,189
- [All] Yabuki, Yabuki, Yabuki!

782
00:30:18,189 --> 00:30:19,991
- Is everything ready for the conference?

783
00:30:19,991 --> 00:30:23,330
- [Tom] Helen of Troy.
- What's the matter?

784
00:30:23,330 --> 00:30:24,519
- [Crow] I'm through making coffee!

785
00:30:24,519 --> 00:30:27,387
- [Yabuki] So you've finally
revealed your true colors.

786
00:30:27,387 --> 00:30:29,072
You're the one who betrayed us.

787
00:30:29,072 --> 00:30:31,356
I'm disappointed in you.

788
00:30:31,356 --> 00:30:34,227
- Accept the proposal they've offered you.

789
00:30:34,227 --> 00:30:36,620
Atari's life in exchange for Mighty Jack.

790
00:30:36,620 --> 00:30:38,720
- [Tom] It's pure beef!

791
00:30:38,720 --> 00:30:40,497
- Unless, Colonel, you
would rather exchange

792
00:30:40,497 --> 00:30:42,385
your life for Mighty Jack?

793
00:30:42,385 --> 00:30:43,868
(laughing)

794
00:30:43,868 --> 00:30:46,236
- [Tom] Woah Gramps, get some Pearl Drops!

795
00:30:46,236 --> 00:30:48,284
(gasps)
- [Crow] Huh?

796
00:30:48,284 --> 00:30:49,117
Oh.

797
00:30:50,736 --> 00:30:53,721
- All right, drop the gun.

798
00:30:53,721 --> 00:30:55,748
- [Crow] I'll just place it very carefully

799
00:30:55,748 --> 00:30:59,581
on the counter and--
(yelling)

800
00:31:00,894 --> 00:31:04,886
- [Tom] She won't get very
far in those cheap pumps.

801
00:31:04,886 --> 00:31:07,136
Feel like a sneaker though.

802
00:31:08,969 --> 00:31:11,753
- [Crow] Sam Spade's office!

803
00:31:11,753 --> 00:31:12,586
Spacious.

804
00:31:14,195 --> 00:31:15,700
- [Tom] Look out, get her!

805
00:31:15,700 --> 00:31:16,841
Manics, stop her!

806
00:31:16,841 --> 00:31:19,425
- [Tom] Hooker's a good cop!

807
00:31:19,425 --> 00:31:20,675
I gotta say it.

808
00:31:24,340 --> 00:31:26,727
Well then, ooh!
(explosion)

809
00:31:26,727 --> 00:31:29,644
- [Crow] Sorry I blew up like that.

810
00:31:31,657 --> 00:31:32,681
- [Joel] Hmm, so?

811
00:31:32,681 --> 00:31:34,181
- She's dead, sir.

812
00:31:35,295 --> 00:31:39,145
I believe she had swallowed
some sort of lethal capsule.

813
00:31:39,145 --> 00:31:39,978
And then it--

814
00:31:39,978 --> 00:31:42,963
- [Tom] Wiggled and Wriggled
and triggered inside her!

815
00:31:42,963 --> 00:31:45,204
- As if it had been triggered
off by remote control.

816
00:31:45,204 --> 00:31:47,621
- [All] The crappy game show?

817
00:31:48,553 --> 00:31:49,791
- [Joel] Okay kids, come on,

818
00:31:49,791 --> 00:31:53,708
it's in or out, close
the screen door, come on!

819
00:31:54,707 --> 00:31:55,967
- [Tom] Ooh.

820
00:31:55,967 --> 00:31:57,204
- [Joel] Woah, looks like it's gettin'

821
00:31:57,204 --> 00:32:01,371
kinda low on baking soda.
- [Crow] Yeah, it happens.

822
00:32:02,315 --> 00:32:04,265
- Come back as soon as
you've scouted the island.

823
00:32:04,265 --> 00:32:06,280
- [Tom] Gotta get this
suit back to Ivan Tors.

824
00:32:06,280 --> 00:32:07,437
- Roger.
- [Tom] Whittaker.

825
00:32:07,437 --> 00:32:08,964
(laughing)

826
00:32:08,964 --> 00:32:13,796
(waves crashing)
(mysterious music)

827
00:32:13,796 --> 00:32:14,797
Wow.

828
00:32:14,797 --> 00:32:17,964
It's the island of Miles Davis!

829
00:32:17,964 --> 00:32:19,331
- [Joel] You know, I
bet he has a perfectly

830
00:32:19,331 --> 00:32:20,836
dry tuxedo under that.

831
00:32:20,836 --> 00:32:24,292
- [Tom] Or a perfectly dry martini.

832
00:32:24,292 --> 00:32:28,209
- [Crow] Glen Corbett,
what are you doin' here?

833
00:32:32,425 --> 00:32:35,711
- [Tom] Oh, it's Aaron Spelling's house.

834
00:32:35,711 --> 00:32:37,252
Akiba!

835
00:32:37,252 --> 00:32:40,973
(mock-Asian vocalizations)

836
00:32:40,973 --> 00:32:42,084
You know, I've always wanted to see

837
00:32:42,084 --> 00:32:44,932
the inside of Bebe Rebozo's house.

838
00:32:44,932 --> 00:32:47,012
(murmuring)

839
00:32:47,012 --> 00:32:47,845
Dick?

840
00:32:49,892 --> 00:32:51,361
- [Joel] Powder blue,

841
00:32:51,361 --> 00:32:54,088
spies ask for it by name.

842
00:32:54,088 --> 00:32:56,505
(whispering)

843
00:33:01,459 --> 00:33:03,804
- [Tom] Somethin' tells
me that Wynton Marsalis

844
00:33:03,804 --> 00:33:05,971
is around the next corner.

845
00:33:08,529 --> 00:33:12,038
- [Crow] Oh Akio, Akio,
wherefore art thou, Akio?

846
00:33:12,038 --> 00:33:14,955
(mysterious music)

847
00:33:17,756 --> 00:33:21,756
Woah, big dog, rottweiler!
- [Tom] Ooh, look out!

848
00:33:23,769 --> 00:33:26,161
- [Joel] It's Teo Macero.

849
00:33:26,161 --> 00:33:28,744
(upbeat music)

850
00:33:31,644 --> 00:33:34,182
- [Jerry] Calling Mighty Jack, it's Jerry.

851
00:33:34,182 --> 00:33:38,148
- Mighty Jack, I see you finally made it.

852
00:33:38,148 --> 00:33:39,461
Where's the installation?

853
00:33:39,461 --> 00:33:41,126
- [Jerry] On the south side of the island.

854
00:33:41,126 --> 00:33:42,469
- How's Atari?
- [Crow] Kind of a jerk,

855
00:33:42,469 --> 00:33:45,951
but he grows on ya.
(Tom chuckles)

856
00:33:45,951 --> 00:33:49,877
- [Tom] And so the male zygote
swims out to meet the egg.

857
00:33:49,877 --> 00:33:51,710
- [Joel] Hey Aqualung.

858
00:33:52,842 --> 00:33:56,509
- [Crow] Navy Seals,
starring Charlie Sheen.

859
00:33:58,703 --> 00:34:01,286
- Hello Mighty Jack,
I'm on the island now.

860
00:34:01,286 --> 00:34:03,037
I'm gonna try and rescue them.

861
00:34:03,037 --> 00:34:03,870
- Yes sir.

862
00:34:05,085 --> 00:34:08,252
- [Joel] I'll just cover my scat here.

863
00:34:09,480 --> 00:34:11,718
- [Tom] Now let's see what we have here.

864
00:34:11,718 --> 00:34:13,085
Chicken leg.

865
00:34:13,085 --> 00:34:15,464
Oh, Kraft singles and
a note from my mother!

866
00:34:15,464 --> 00:34:17,297
"I'm so proud of you."

867
00:34:20,571 --> 00:34:23,406
- [Crow] What is that, a
pool cue or a silencer?

868
00:34:23,406 --> 00:34:26,087
Just put that part on,
that makes it loud again.

869
00:34:26,087 --> 00:34:27,474
Oh, and that attachment for the

870
00:34:27,474 --> 00:34:29,891
hard-to-reach assassinations.

871
00:34:31,122 --> 00:34:32,871
How many silencers does he need?

872
00:34:32,871 --> 00:34:34,621
- [Tom] I don't know.

873
00:34:36,698 --> 00:34:37,889
Well, you know, these fern prisons

874
00:34:37,889 --> 00:34:40,096
were really popular in
the 70s, weren't they?

875
00:34:40,096 --> 00:34:41,313
- [Joel] Natch.

876
00:34:41,313 --> 00:34:42,480
- [Crow] Puma?

877
00:34:44,319 --> 00:34:45,419
- [Tom] Dad?

878
00:34:45,419 --> 00:34:46,709
- [Joel] Watch out for that

879
00:34:46,709 --> 00:34:49,959
palm leaf!
(vocalizing)

880
00:34:51,883 --> 00:34:53,931
- [Tom] I will succeed where he failed.

881
00:34:53,931 --> 00:34:54,849
- Jerry?

882
00:34:54,849 --> 00:34:55,755
Where are you?

883
00:34:55,755 --> 00:34:59,581
- [Crow] Oh hello Mr.
Rescue Person I'm in...

884
00:34:59,581 --> 00:35:00,721
- [Jerry] It's the door on the right.

885
00:35:00,721 --> 00:35:01,691
- Okay.

886
00:35:01,691 --> 00:35:04,441
- [Joel] It's by the ice machine.

887
00:35:06,587 --> 00:35:07,737
- [Crow] I have a feeling that

888
00:35:07,737 --> 00:35:10,715
kooky chaos is about to ensue.

889
00:35:10,715 --> 00:35:13,237
- [Tom] It's the M. C. Escher house!

890
00:35:13,237 --> 00:35:16,737
Escher house!
(vocalizing)

891
00:35:20,724 --> 00:35:23,327
(knocking)
- [Joel] Room service!

892
00:35:23,327 --> 00:35:24,415
- [Jerry] That you, Captain?

893
00:35:24,415 --> 00:35:25,915
The door's locked!

894
00:35:29,374 --> 00:35:32,063
- [Crow] Oh, thanks for knocking, Dean!

895
00:35:32,063 --> 00:35:33,727
- They're trying to
kill us with poison gas!

896
00:35:33,727 --> 00:35:35,310
- [Tom] Who, Exxon?

897
00:35:36,372 --> 00:35:37,689
- [Crow] Aw, that'll help a lot.

898
00:35:37,689 --> 00:35:39,405
- Hold still, it's
better if you don't move!

899
00:35:39,405 --> 00:35:40,803
- We've got to get out, I'm choking.

900
00:35:40,803 --> 00:35:43,581
- [Joel] I saved my handkerchief.

901
00:35:43,581 --> 00:35:45,981
(gagging)

902
00:35:45,981 --> 00:35:48,314
It's here in my espadrilles.

903
00:35:51,378 --> 00:35:52,850
(snaps)
(explosion)

904
00:35:52,850 --> 00:35:55,176
- [Tom] It's a snap!

905
00:35:55,176 --> 00:35:56,722
- Come on!

906
00:35:56,722 --> 00:35:58,889
(gasping)

907
00:36:02,162 --> 00:36:04,018
- [Atari] Wait!

908
00:36:04,018 --> 00:36:07,122
Before we go, we ought
to blow the place up.

909
00:36:07,122 --> 00:36:11,289
- [Crow] That's great, why
didn't you tell us that before?

910
00:36:13,810 --> 00:36:16,008
- Okay, let's do it.
- [Tom] Let's fall in love!

911
00:36:16,008 --> 00:36:17,160
- Jerry.

912
00:36:17,160 --> 00:36:18,397
Return to Mighty Jack.

913
00:36:18,397 --> 00:36:19,389
- What about you?

914
00:36:19,389 --> 00:36:21,358
- I've got the buggy here.
- [Jerry] But Captain!

915
00:36:21,358 --> 00:36:22,850
- That's an order!

916
00:36:22,850 --> 00:36:24,301
- Yes sir.

917
00:36:24,301 --> 00:36:27,801
- [Joel] He never lets me drive the buggy.

918
00:36:29,463 --> 00:36:30,905
- [Atari] Don't move!

919
00:36:30,905 --> 00:36:32,863
- [Crow] You moved!

920
00:36:32,863 --> 00:36:34,076
Hey, give me a turn at that!

921
00:36:34,076 --> 00:36:36,081
Woo, it's fun!
(laughing)

922
00:36:36,081 --> 00:36:39,356
- Right, let's go.
- [Tenda] Right.

923
00:36:39,356 --> 00:36:41,242
(explosions)

924
00:36:41,242 --> 00:36:43,659
- [Tom] Yeah.
- [Joel] Unreal.

925
00:36:46,278 --> 00:36:47,868
- [Crow] Ooh.

926
00:36:47,868 --> 00:36:50,169
- [Tom] Ooh, pretty.

927
00:36:50,169 --> 00:36:54,022
- [Joel] They sound
like horses, don't they?

928
00:36:54,022 --> 00:36:56,003
- [Tom] What do we got, a Volkswagen?

929
00:36:56,003 --> 00:36:57,825
- [Crow] Oh great, good thing there

930
00:36:57,825 --> 00:36:59,704
happened to be a chopper around!

931
00:36:59,704 --> 00:37:02,091
(Tom chuckles)
(helicopter blades whirring)

932
00:37:02,091 --> 00:37:04,323
- [Tom] Traffic over the
Pacific Ocean is light today,

933
00:37:04,323 --> 00:37:07,128
expect no delays between
Mindanao and Hawaii.

934
00:37:07,128 --> 00:37:10,689
- [Joel] Looks like the
Tidy Bowl man traded up.

935
00:37:10,689 --> 00:37:12,301
The water's blue.

936
00:37:12,301 --> 00:37:15,468
(helicopter whirring)

937
00:37:17,283 --> 00:37:19,683
- [Tom] Were informal at
Mighty Jack here, Steve.

938
00:37:19,683 --> 00:37:21,516
- [Crow] Shirtsleeves.

939
00:37:30,334 --> 00:37:32,130
- [Tom] Well then, down the hatch!

940
00:37:32,130 --> 00:37:34,040
Orrin Hatch!
(laughing)

941
00:37:34,040 --> 00:37:36,771
Little joke for our
friends in Utah, Senator.

942
00:37:36,771 --> 00:37:39,854
Fine, distinguished colleague from...

943
00:37:42,947 --> 00:37:44,973
- All right, engines on!
- [Jerry] Yes sir!

944
00:37:44,973 --> 00:37:46,951
- [Tenda] Combat stations!

945
00:37:46,951 --> 00:37:48,872
- [Crow] Boy, just think
if this movie had a plot.

946
00:37:48,872 --> 00:37:51,705
Might really be neat.
- [Tom] Yeah.

947
00:37:57,658 --> 00:37:59,408
- [Joel] Neat decals.

948
00:38:00,462 --> 00:38:02,129
Excellent detailing.

949
00:38:03,267 --> 00:38:05,100
- [Tom] Wait a minute!

950
00:38:06,947 --> 00:38:09,827
- [Crow] Sherwood Schwarz
presents, Gilligan's Island 2000!

951
00:38:09,827 --> 00:38:12,952
With Gilligan, the Admiral too.

952
00:38:12,952 --> 00:38:14,285
The billionaire.

953
00:38:15,907 --> 00:38:17,027
- [Tom] Weenie launch.

954
00:38:17,027 --> 00:38:18,194
Weenie launch.

955
00:38:19,779 --> 00:38:21,911
(explosions)

956
00:38:21,911 --> 00:38:22,994
- [Joel] Wow!

957
00:38:25,558 --> 00:38:26,391
No!

958
00:38:28,845 --> 00:38:30,700
- [Crow] Oh no, they hit the Howells' hut!

959
00:38:30,700 --> 00:38:32,952
Lovey, I'm on fire!

960
00:38:32,952 --> 00:38:35,119
- [Tom] Flash.
- [All] Ahh!

961
00:38:36,845 --> 00:38:40,262
- [Tom] Gets tiring after a while though.

962
00:38:41,679 --> 00:38:43,324
Apocalypse Now?

963
00:38:43,324 --> 00:38:44,574
Apocalypse Not!

964
00:38:47,276 --> 00:38:49,483
- [Joel] December 7th, 2041,

965
00:38:49,483 --> 00:38:52,795
a film that will live in infamy!

966
00:38:52,795 --> 00:38:53,927
- [Tom] Oh look, the mosquito.

967
00:38:53,927 --> 00:38:56,359
Minnesota's state bird.
(Tom chuckles)

968
00:38:56,359 --> 00:38:57,578
For our friends in Minnesota.

969
00:38:57,578 --> 00:38:58,745
Weenie launch.

970
00:39:00,501 --> 00:39:02,336
- [Joel] Crest.

971
00:39:02,336 --> 00:39:03,753
- [All] Ooh, ooh!

972
00:39:04,693 --> 00:39:06,272
Ahh!
(clapping)

973
00:39:06,272 --> 00:39:08,084
- [Tom] Oh, beautiful.

974
00:39:08,084 --> 00:39:09,685
- [Crow] It's a Memphis Belle!

975
00:39:09,685 --> 00:39:12,816
Another dumb movie.
- [All] Ooh, ahh!

976
00:39:12,816 --> 00:39:15,399
- [Joel] Wow.
- [Tom] Beautiful.

977
00:39:16,664 --> 00:39:19,848
- [Crow] They're using
every toy in the box!

978
00:39:19,848 --> 00:39:21,811
- [Joel] Here comes the grand finale.

979
00:39:21,811 --> 00:39:24,311
- Full thrust!
- [Crow] Really?

980
00:39:25,427 --> 00:39:26,603
Gamera!

981
00:39:26,603 --> 00:39:27,436
Oh, sorry.

982
00:39:28,891 --> 00:39:30,565
- [Tom] From the fun and
sun capital of the world,

983
00:39:30,565 --> 00:39:32,315
Miami Beach, comes...

984
00:39:35,298 --> 00:39:36,533
- [Crow] You know, the
Tommy Bartlett Show's

985
00:39:36,533 --> 00:39:39,061
really getting expensive.

986
00:39:39,061 --> 00:39:40,395
- [Tom] Now we see here where the

987
00:39:40,395 --> 00:39:43,478
patriot missiles intercept the Scuds.

988
00:39:46,482 --> 00:39:47,315
And...

989
00:39:48,523 --> 00:39:49,440
Woah!

990
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:51,659
- [Crow] God bless the patriot missiles!

991
00:39:51,659 --> 00:39:52,864
- [Tom] And we'd like to welcome you

992
00:39:52,864 --> 00:39:54,784
to Collateral Damage Playhouse.

993
00:39:54,784 --> 00:39:57,201
(explosions)

994
00:39:58,304 --> 00:39:59,387
- [Joel] Wow.

995
00:40:03,562 --> 00:40:06,094
- [Crow] Did you do that?
- [Jerry] Let's go after them!

996
00:40:06,094 --> 00:40:07,035
- It's no use.

997
00:40:07,035 --> 00:40:09,467
Their speed is much faster than ours.

998
00:40:09,467 --> 00:40:10,597
- I can't believe it!

999
00:40:10,597 --> 00:40:11,920
Faster than Mighty Jack?

1000
00:40:11,920 --> 00:40:13,275
- Never underrate your enemy.

1001
00:40:13,275 --> 00:40:15,003
- [Joel] I think that's
how it goes, isn't it?

1002
00:40:15,003 --> 00:40:17,988
- Anyway, we saved Mr. Atari
and that's all that matters.

1003
00:40:17,988 --> 00:40:19,600
- Captain.

1004
00:40:19,600 --> 00:40:21,979
I think we ought to destroy
the island completely.

1005
00:40:21,979 --> 00:40:24,315
- [Crow] Okay, Mr. Manifest Destiny.

1006
00:40:24,315 --> 00:40:26,505
- Tommy, let's go back to the island.

1007
00:40:26,505 --> 00:40:28,005
- [Tommy] Yes sir.

1008
00:40:28,981 --> 00:40:30,481
- [Tom] Bank turn.

1009
00:40:33,427 --> 00:40:35,594
(humming)

1010
00:40:37,373 --> 00:40:38,685
♫ Accidents will-- ♫

1011
00:40:38,685 --> 00:40:39,912
Huh?

1012
00:40:39,912 --> 00:40:40,893
- I don't like that guy.

1013
00:40:40,893 --> 00:40:41,875
Who does he think he is?

1014
00:40:41,875 --> 00:40:44,851
- Careful, he might hear ya, he's a VIP.

1015
00:40:44,851 --> 00:40:46,035
- Yeah, ya don't say.

1016
00:40:46,035 --> 00:40:47,293
We risk our necks to save his life

1017
00:40:47,293 --> 00:40:48,648
and now he's giving orders.

1018
00:40:48,648 --> 00:40:49,672
- [Tom] Hey, nice hat!

1019
00:40:49,672 --> 00:40:51,624
- We'll be over the target very soon.

1020
00:40:51,624 --> 00:40:52,829
- Say, Captain.

1021
00:40:52,829 --> 00:40:54,365
Should we drop a few bombs?

1022
00:40:54,365 --> 00:40:56,317
It'll keep them quiet for a while.

1023
00:40:56,317 --> 00:40:57,150
- Good idea.

1024
00:40:57,150 --> 00:41:00,498
- [Tom] That's what Kissinger would do.

1025
00:41:00,498 --> 00:41:02,940
(explosions)

1026
00:41:02,940 --> 00:41:03,773
Oops.

1027
00:41:05,472 --> 00:41:09,588
- [Joel] Hey, that's a
baby formula factory!

1028
00:41:09,588 --> 00:41:13,953
- [Tom] Ah, Tet, my
favorite holiday, you know?

1029
00:41:13,953 --> 00:41:16,235
- [Joel] There goes the
Ken and Barbie dream home!

1030
00:41:16,235 --> 00:41:17,708
- [Tom] Ooh!

1031
00:41:17,708 --> 00:41:20,125
(explosions)

1032
00:41:23,910 --> 00:41:25,836
Oh no, not the AM radio towers!

1033
00:41:25,836 --> 00:41:28,780
(mumbling)

1034
00:41:28,780 --> 00:41:30,636
- [Crow] God, I love the
smell of burning flesh

1035
00:41:30,636 --> 00:41:32,193
and the sound of breaking glass!

1036
00:41:32,193 --> 00:41:33,276
- [Joel] Ooh!

1037
00:41:36,108 --> 00:41:38,785
- [Tom] Well then.
- Mission accomplished.

1038
00:41:38,785 --> 00:41:40,780
Now let's go home.

1039
00:41:40,780 --> 00:41:42,337
- [Tom] The Wimbledon judges agree.

1040
00:41:42,337 --> 00:41:44,587
(laughing)

1041
00:41:46,966 --> 00:41:48,466
- [Crow] Dickweed.

1042
00:41:49,868 --> 00:41:50,701
Tag.

1043
00:41:52,527 --> 00:41:54,275
- [Joel] Oh boy, here comes another--

1044
00:41:54,275 --> 00:41:55,686
- [All] Bank turn.

1045
00:41:55,686 --> 00:41:57,318
- [Joel] How many more you gotta look at?

1046
00:41:57,318 --> 00:42:00,038
- [Voiceover] You have not
destroyed us, Mighty Jack!

1047
00:42:00,038 --> 00:42:02,001
We will retaliate for this!

1048
00:42:02,001 --> 00:42:04,134
Our organization is powerful!

1049
00:42:04,134 --> 00:42:07,643
Q will return and annihilate you forever!

1050
00:42:07,643 --> 00:42:10,417
- [Joel] But first, these
messages from Crest.

1051
00:42:10,417 --> 00:42:11,473
- [Crow] Yeah yeah, we all live

1052
00:42:11,473 --> 00:42:14,364
in a yellow submarine, we know.

1053
00:42:14,364 --> 00:42:16,550
♫ Super slow

1054
00:42:16,550 --> 00:42:18,236
♫ Moving car

1055
00:42:18,236 --> 00:42:22,236
♫ Super slow ♫

1056
00:42:25,839 --> 00:42:28,803
- [Tom] Meanwhile, at the
movie's biggest phallic symbol...

1057
00:42:28,803 --> 00:42:31,736
- [Joel] Hey, pull my finger.

1058
00:42:31,736 --> 00:42:32,951
- [Crow] Aw, Jeannie's really done it

1059
00:42:32,951 --> 00:42:34,951
this time, Major Healey.

1060
00:42:39,747 --> 00:42:41,624
- [Tom] I'm going out,
anybody need anything?

1061
00:42:41,624 --> 00:42:44,452
- Finally made it back to base,

1062
00:42:44,452 --> 00:42:46,130
and we're not allowed to get off.

1063
00:42:46,130 --> 00:42:48,317
- Those were the orders from headquarters.

1064
00:42:48,317 --> 00:42:51,186
- [Tom] Poor guy.
(vocalizing)

1065
00:42:51,186 --> 00:42:53,517
- [Joel] Woah, the chicks are here!

1066
00:42:53,517 --> 00:42:54,946
(laughing)

1067
00:42:54,946 --> 00:42:56,088
- Welcome back, Jerry!

1068
00:42:56,088 --> 00:42:58,136
The mission was successful, wasn't it?

1069
00:42:58,136 --> 00:42:59,522
- Yeah, but I didn't enjoy it.

1070
00:42:59,522 --> 00:43:01,965
- [Crow] Oh, and that's all that matters.

1071
00:43:01,965 --> 00:43:04,301
- Well, ya see, there was this guy.

1072
00:43:04,301 --> 00:43:05,933
I just couldn't stand him.

1073
00:43:05,933 --> 00:43:06,933
- [Tom] Ooh.

1074
00:43:08,039 --> 00:43:08,872
Doh!

1075
00:43:08,872 --> 00:43:11,506
- [Crow] Ask not what your
country can do for you...

1076
00:43:11,506 --> 00:43:14,045
(gasping)

1077
00:43:14,045 --> 00:43:16,509
- Allow me to introduce...

1078
00:43:16,509 --> 00:43:18,066
Major Harold Atari.

1079
00:43:18,066 --> 00:43:20,316
- [All] Whomp whomp whomp..

1080
00:43:22,199 --> 00:43:24,599
- [Crow] Open mouth, insert foot.

1081
00:43:24,599 --> 00:43:27,863
(Tom chuckles)

1082
00:43:27,863 --> 00:43:28,914
- [Tom] Akiba.

1083
00:43:28,914 --> 00:43:30,386
- Welcome aboard.

1084
00:43:30,386 --> 00:43:31,600
Commander.

1085
00:43:31,600 --> 00:43:33,665
- The captain is your Executive Officer.

1086
00:43:33,665 --> 00:43:35,268
- [Tom] He'll be kissing
up to you right away.

1087
00:43:35,268 --> 00:43:36,785
- Captain.

1088
00:43:36,785 --> 00:43:38,725
- It's an honor, sir.

1089
00:43:38,725 --> 00:43:41,303
- [Crow] You've got a cute smile.

1090
00:43:41,303 --> 00:43:42,614
- Lieutenant Jerry.

1091
00:43:42,614 --> 00:43:45,367
- [Crow] Oh with the thing, I'm sorry.

1092
00:43:45,367 --> 00:43:46,263
- It's good to see ya.

1093
00:43:46,263 --> 00:43:48,129
I'd like to thank you for rescuing me.

1094
00:43:48,129 --> 00:43:49,953
- Oh, it was nothing.
(Tom stammering)

1095
00:43:49,953 --> 00:43:51,575
- If you hadn't come...

1096
00:43:51,575 --> 00:43:52,908
- [Joel] Oh, we're off.

1097
00:43:52,908 --> 00:43:55,821
- [Tom] Oh, we should get going.

1098
00:43:55,821 --> 00:43:57,798
- [Crow] I'll miss the plot!
- [Joel] I don't know...

1099
00:43:57,798 --> 00:43:58,652
- [Voiceover] With its new Commander,

1100
00:43:58,652 --> 00:44:00,850
the Mighty Jack team is complete.

1101
00:44:00,850 --> 00:44:03,433
(upbeat music)

1102
00:44:06,935 --> 00:44:08,352
- Guys, hey guys!

1103
00:44:09,192 --> 00:44:12,451
Hey, I knew you were gonna do this to me!

1104
00:44:12,451 --> 00:44:14,083
Would you get this thing off my head?

1105
00:44:14,083 --> 00:44:15,651
- Silence!
- [Crow] Meow!

1106
00:44:15,651 --> 00:44:17,057
- Thank you, there there, Flopsy.

1107
00:44:17,057 --> 00:44:18,840
You had better tell me
what I want to know.

1108
00:44:18,840 --> 00:44:21,176
The lights in there are
capable of blinding you!

1109
00:44:21,176 --> 00:44:22,733
- [Joel] Oh that doesn't bother me,

1110
00:44:22,733 --> 00:44:24,397
I'll just keep my eyes shut.

1111
00:44:24,397 --> 00:44:26,611
- Doh, foiled again!
- [Crow] Boy, is he smart!

1112
00:44:26,611 --> 00:44:28,168
- [Tom] Hey you can say
that, would you knock it off?

1113
00:44:28,168 --> 00:44:29,203
You're supposed to be a cat!
- [Crow] Ah, meow!

1114
00:44:29,203 --> 00:44:31,286
- Thank you.
- [Crow] Sure.

1115
00:44:31,286 --> 00:44:33,558
- [Joel] Hey, would you guys
hurry up, it's hot in here!

1116
00:44:33,558 --> 00:44:35,469
- Joel, aren't you just the tiniest bit

1117
00:44:35,469 --> 00:44:37,357
curious about those blinding lights?

1118
00:44:37,357 --> 00:44:39,245
Don't you want to peek, just a little bit?

1119
00:44:39,245 --> 00:44:40,392
- [Joel] No!

1120
00:44:40,392 --> 00:44:41,832
- Hey, like I said, he's smart!

1121
00:44:41,832 --> 00:44:43,795
- Oh boy, guess all of
those swimsuit posters

1122
00:44:43,795 --> 00:44:44,822
on the wall are going to go

1123
00:44:44,822 --> 00:44:46,351
completely to waste, aren't they?

1124
00:44:46,351 --> 00:44:47,928
- And I guess you wouldn't
even be interested

1125
00:44:47,928 --> 00:44:50,607
in that rare Paul Clay
painting on the wall either?

1126
00:44:50,607 --> 00:44:53,338
- [Joel] Oh, you guys don't
have a Paul Clay painting.

1127
00:44:53,338 --> 00:44:54,522
- Boy, is he smart.

1128
00:44:54,522 --> 00:44:55,908
- Yeah, the guy is smart.

1129
00:44:55,908 --> 00:44:57,923
- Aren't you supposed to be my cat?

1130
00:44:57,923 --> 00:44:59,006
- Um, meow.
- [Tom] Thank you!

1131
00:44:59,006 --> 00:45:00,214
- Sure.

1132
00:45:00,214 --> 00:45:01,068
- Oh, I've got an idea!

1133
00:45:01,068 --> 00:45:04,571
Joel, I seem to have
misplaced the Hope Diamond.

1134
00:45:04,571 --> 00:45:05,692
Would you look around in there for me?

1135
00:45:05,692 --> 00:45:06,993
- [Joel] Oh, it's not in here.

1136
00:45:06,993 --> 00:45:08,391
- Well, did you even look?

1137
00:45:08,391 --> 00:45:09,841
- [Joel] No, I'm not going to!

1138
00:45:09,841 --> 00:45:11,687
- Boy is he smart.
- [Crow] Smart is the word.

1139
00:45:11,687 --> 00:45:13,189
(chanting)

1140
00:45:13,189 --> 00:45:14,759
Joel, I hate to get tough,

1141
00:45:14,759 --> 00:45:19,418
but inside that box with
you is a poison sandwich!

1142
00:45:19,418 --> 00:45:20,454
- [Joel] I just won't eat it.

1143
00:45:20,454 --> 00:45:21,983
- Oh, foiled again!

1144
00:45:21,983 --> 00:45:23,756
- You've completely lost
that cat thing, haven't you?

1145
00:45:23,756 --> 00:45:25,185
- I admit it, I'm way off script,

1146
00:45:25,185 --> 00:45:26,695
I've got no idea what I'm doing.

1147
00:45:26,695 --> 00:45:28,241
- [Joel] Oh guys, come on!

1148
00:45:28,241 --> 00:45:29,617
- What are you...

1149
00:45:29,617 --> 00:45:31,452
- It's so uncomfortable in there.

1150
00:45:31,452 --> 00:45:32,923
- Oh, has the great Joel Robinson

1151
00:45:32,923 --> 00:45:35,431
decided fun time is over now?

1152
00:45:35,431 --> 00:45:36,391
- Man, what's the matter--

1153
00:45:36,391 --> 00:45:38,768
- Oh, so Joel, don't say hi!
- [Crow] Meow.

1154
00:45:38,768 --> 00:45:41,057
- You have got to be kidding me Crow!

1155
00:45:41,057 --> 00:45:43,137
- Hey Crow, you wanna go
get some frozen yogurt--

1156
00:45:43,137 --> 00:45:46,519
(buzzing)
(yelling)

1157
00:45:46,519 --> 00:45:49,186
(doors opening)

1158
00:45:55,640 --> 00:45:57,371
- [Joel] Oh, my cigarettes are ringing.

1159
00:45:57,371 --> 00:45:58,877
- [Tom] Think you're so smart.

1160
00:45:58,877 --> 00:46:01,377
- [Crow] Meow?
- [Tom] Shut up.

1161
00:46:02,215 --> 00:46:03,175
- Atari here.

1162
00:46:03,175 --> 00:46:04,167
- [Yabuki] We have problems.

1163
00:46:04,167 --> 00:46:05,000
- What?

1164
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:07,516
- [Yabuki] They've
destroyed the installation.

1165
00:46:07,516 --> 00:46:08,847
- [Tom] We'll have to
re-carpet everything.

1166
00:46:08,847 --> 00:46:09,893
- The official island's gone?

1167
00:46:09,893 --> 00:46:11,602
- [Yabuki] Yes.

1168
00:46:11,602 --> 00:46:12,769
I'm afraid so.

1169
00:46:14,199 --> 00:46:15,381
- It's Q again.

1170
00:46:15,381 --> 00:46:17,068
- [Crow] Nothing compares to Q.

1171
00:46:17,068 --> 00:46:19,786
- We urgently need titanium alloy

1172
00:46:19,786 --> 00:46:22,945
for a top-priority
military research project.

1173
00:46:22,945 --> 00:46:24,481
- [Joel] Got any in your junk drawer?

1174
00:46:24,481 --> 00:46:28,096
- How soon can you be
ready for redeployment?

1175
00:46:28,096 --> 00:46:29,127
- Well, let's see.

1176
00:46:29,127 --> 00:46:30,683
I have to shave and then I'll want

1177
00:46:30,683 --> 00:46:33,168
to eat a decent breakfast of toast,

1178
00:46:33,168 --> 00:46:35,655
scrambled eggs and black coffee.

1179
00:46:35,655 --> 00:46:37,248
- [Crow] That's
fascinating, get over here!

1180
00:46:37,248 --> 00:46:39,637
- If that's the case, take your time.

1181
00:46:39,637 --> 00:46:41,887
(laughing)

1182
00:46:43,456 --> 00:46:44,971
- [Atari] And don't forget I want--

1183
00:46:44,971 --> 00:46:47,776
- [Joel] Ooh!
- [Tom] Really gets me off.

1184
00:46:47,776 --> 00:46:49,943
- [All] Whomp whomp whomp.

1185
00:46:50,791 --> 00:46:52,112
- [Atari] I'll have some orange juice.

1186
00:46:52,112 --> 00:46:54,249
- [Voiceover] Yes sir.
(tom laughing)

1187
00:46:54,249 --> 00:46:57,782
- [Tom] Oh that razzie son of a gun.

1188
00:46:57,782 --> 00:46:59,976
- [Atari] Engines on?
- Engines on!

1189
00:46:59,976 --> 00:47:02,642
- [Joel] And strap your
hands across my engines!

1190
00:47:02,642 --> 00:47:03,899
- [Crow] Toast is ready, sir.

1191
00:47:03,899 --> 00:47:05,328
- Ready for submerging.

1192
00:47:05,328 --> 00:47:09,071
- Submerge!
- [Crew Member] Submerge.

1193
00:47:09,071 --> 00:47:11,238
- [Joel] I said dry toast.

1194
00:47:13,894 --> 00:47:15,846
- [Tom] How are we on
the about this big meter?

1195
00:47:15,846 --> 00:47:18,320
- [Crew Member] Water level, 50 feet.

1196
00:47:18,320 --> 00:47:19,609
- Unlock gates.

1197
00:47:19,609 --> 00:47:20,838
- Unlock gates!

1198
00:47:20,838 --> 00:47:22,672
- [Joel] Daryl Gates,
David Gates and Brett...

1199
00:47:22,672 --> 00:47:24,368
There's the toast thing again.

1200
00:47:24,368 --> 00:47:26,630
- [Tom] What's with the toast?

1201
00:47:26,630 --> 00:47:28,603
- [Crow] Why'd they
fly through the window?

1202
00:47:28,603 --> 00:47:30,128
- [Tom] We've replaced the Pacific Ocean

1203
00:47:30,128 --> 00:47:33,128
with Folgers' crystals, let's watch.

1204
00:47:35,430 --> 00:47:37,584
- We'll first search the
area in the Arctic zone.

1205
00:47:37,584 --> 00:47:38,417
- [All] Yes sir!

1206
00:47:38,417 --> 00:47:41,328
- [Joel] Open the Venetian blinds!

1207
00:47:41,328 --> 00:47:42,220
- [Mary] On course, sir.

1208
00:47:42,220 --> 00:47:44,594
- What's our present speed?

1209
00:47:44,594 --> 00:47:45,447
- Mach two.

1210
00:47:45,447 --> 00:47:47,858
- [Tom] I've got a Mac Classic.

1211
00:47:47,858 --> 00:47:49,319
- [Atari] Maintain speed and proceed

1212
00:47:49,319 --> 00:47:51,164
in the direction north, northwest.

1213
00:47:51,164 --> 00:47:52,860
- [Crow] See if James Mason is there.

1214
00:47:52,860 --> 00:47:54,482
- [Tom] North By Northwest.

1215
00:47:54,482 --> 00:47:55,505
- [Crow] It's kind of a stretch.

1216
00:47:55,505 --> 00:47:57,179
- [Joel] Enough with the bank turns!

1217
00:47:57,179 --> 00:47:58,491
- [Tom] Really!

1218
00:47:58,491 --> 00:48:00,838
(folksy music)

1219
00:48:00,838 --> 00:48:04,507
♫ You ain't woman enough
to take my Mighty Jack

1220
00:48:04,507 --> 00:48:07,301
♫ Yeehoo ♫

1221
00:48:07,301 --> 00:48:09,281
- [Crow] Wow, it's the cover of Dianetics!

1222
00:48:09,281 --> 00:48:13,025
- [Joel] And another bank
turn, thank you very much.

1223
00:48:13,025 --> 00:48:17,659
They're chasing that bright,
elusive butterfly of love.

1224
00:48:17,659 --> 00:48:18,665
- [Joel] Kyle MacLachlan!

1225
00:48:18,665 --> 00:48:22,017
- [Tom] You know, it's
really good today, isn't it?

1226
00:48:22,017 --> 00:48:23,638
They're all enjoying it.

1227
00:48:23,638 --> 00:48:26,026
- Sir, what's that?

1228
00:48:26,026 --> 00:48:28,710
- [Crow] Ha, made ya look!

1229
00:48:28,710 --> 00:48:30,427
- [Tom] Oh, that's just the set of Orca.

1230
00:48:30,427 --> 00:48:32,006
- [Jerry] Oh, it's just an iceberg.

1231
00:48:32,006 --> 00:48:35,104
- We'll be at the North
Pole in five minutes.

1232
00:48:35,104 --> 00:48:36,374
(Tom chuckles)

1233
00:48:36,374 --> 00:48:38,614
- [Tom] Santa Claus gonna be there?

1234
00:48:38,614 --> 00:48:40,203
- [Crow] Hey, it's Ice Station Zebra!

1235
00:48:40,203 --> 00:48:42,038
And look, Howard Hughes is
in his drawstring shorts

1236
00:48:42,038 --> 00:48:44,417
and he's got a mason jar filled--

1237
00:48:44,417 --> 00:48:45,871
(ominous music)

1238
00:48:45,871 --> 00:48:48,538
(evil laughter)

1239
00:48:49,936 --> 00:48:51,019
- [Tom] Neat.

1240
00:48:53,552 --> 00:48:55,219
Evil Good Humor men!

1241
00:48:56,473 --> 00:48:57,828
- [Villain] Enemy approaching.

1242
00:48:57,828 --> 00:49:00,271
Prepare to launch missiles, pronto!

1243
00:49:00,271 --> 00:49:02,297
- [Joel] Oh, he's an Italian.

1244
00:49:02,297 --> 00:49:04,547
- [Tom] What about allegro?

1245
00:49:11,033 --> 00:49:13,134
- The enemy had now gone!

1246
00:49:13,134 --> 00:49:16,895
Close missile sites.
(Crow meows)

1247
00:49:16,895 --> 00:49:18,879
- [Crow] Freezer door won't close.

1248
00:49:18,879 --> 00:49:21,129
They really should defrost.

1249
00:49:22,271 --> 00:49:24,223
- That was Q all right.

1250
00:49:24,223 --> 00:49:26,612
A clever hiding place.
- [Tom] Until spring hits.

1251
00:49:26,612 --> 00:49:28,980
- We'll just wait until
we're ready to attack.

1252
00:49:28,980 --> 00:49:31,063
- [Joel] What a blowhard.

1253
00:49:32,500 --> 00:49:35,551
- Our first duty is to go
inspect the frozen island.

1254
00:49:35,551 --> 00:49:36,479
- [Joel] And then figure out why

1255
00:49:36,479 --> 00:49:39,229
the Howell's had so much luggage.

1256
00:49:40,265 --> 00:49:41,932
- [Crow] I'm Batman.

1257
00:49:44,575 --> 00:49:47,092
- [Tom] You see, that boat
must have very low fat content.

1258
00:49:47,092 --> 00:49:48,009
- [Joel] Now why do you say that?

1259
00:49:48,009 --> 00:49:49,988
- [Tom] Goin' right to the bottom.

1260
00:49:49,988 --> 00:49:52,196
- There's no trace of the
station at the bottom of the sea,

1261
00:49:52,196 --> 00:49:54,063
maybe they succeeded in floating it.

1262
00:49:54,063 --> 00:49:55,087
- [Joel] How's the goatee coming?

1263
00:49:55,087 --> 00:49:56,964
- The could've removed
it in separate sections.

1264
00:49:56,964 --> 00:49:59,611
- Yes, though I don't think
they had time to dismantle it.

1265
00:49:59,611 --> 00:50:00,761
- [Crow] Hey, how ya doin'?

1266
00:50:00,761 --> 00:50:02,607
- Eddie, Yuri?
- [Eddie And Yuri] Yes sir?

1267
00:50:02,607 --> 00:50:05,097
- Put on your diving suits
and scout the whole area.

1268
00:50:05,097 --> 00:50:05,930
- [Both] Yes sir!

1269
00:50:05,930 --> 00:50:06,763
- [Crow] You, put on your diving suit

1270
00:50:06,763 --> 00:50:08,805
and meet me in my cabin.

1271
00:50:08,805 --> 00:50:10,286
- [Atari] Keep radio contact.
- [Mary] Yes sir!

1272
00:50:10,286 --> 00:50:11,385
- [Tom] Somebody else say yes sir!

1273
00:50:11,385 --> 00:50:13,030
- [Joel] Yes sir!
- [Tom] Thank you.

1274
00:50:13,030 --> 00:50:15,694
- [All] Toy diver, toy diver.

1275
00:50:15,694 --> 00:50:17,706
- [Tom] It's Toy Donahue!
(Tom chuckles)

1276
00:50:17,706 --> 00:50:18,789
It's a toy...

1277
00:50:21,182 --> 00:50:22,015
Sorry.

1278
00:50:23,113 --> 00:50:25,321
- [Crow] Flipper is made of liquid metal.

1279
00:50:25,321 --> 00:50:27,988
(ominous music)

1280
00:50:31,518 --> 00:50:33,182
- [Tom] Oh wow man,
they're swimming right to

1281
00:50:33,182 --> 00:50:36,182
Robert Schuller's Crystal Cathedral!

1282
00:50:37,067 --> 00:50:38,317
- Oh, look sir!

1283
00:50:43,953 --> 00:50:46,178
- Load the rockets!

1284
00:50:46,178 --> 00:50:48,345
(pinging)

1285
00:50:49,708 --> 00:50:51,269
- [Joel] Woah, jet-propelled bluegills,

1286
00:50:51,269 --> 00:50:53,932
I read about 'em in Field and Stream!

1287
00:50:53,932 --> 00:50:55,372
- Fire!

1288
00:50:55,372 --> 00:50:56,205
- Yes sir!

1289
00:50:59,671 --> 00:51:02,434
- [Tom] Uh-oh.
- [Crow] Look out!

1290
00:51:02,434 --> 00:51:04,851
(explosions)

1291
00:51:06,018 --> 00:51:07,394
- A direct hit!
- [Tom] With a bullet!

1292
00:51:07,394 --> 00:51:08,844
Goin' right to the top of the charts!

1293
00:51:08,844 --> 00:51:11,490
- Larry, reload rockets!
- [Larry] Yes sir!

1294
00:51:11,490 --> 00:51:13,228
- Mary, keep tracking them.
- [Mary] Yes sir!

1295
00:51:13,228 --> 00:51:14,935
- [Joel] Barry, you grab Mary!
- [Tom] Yes sir!

1296
00:51:14,935 --> 00:51:17,830
- I think one of them's hurt!

1297
00:51:17,830 --> 00:51:21,896
- [Joel] When models goose
themselves, next on Geraldo!

1298
00:51:21,896 --> 00:51:23,481
- Laser gun!
- [Jerry] Laser gun!

1299
00:51:23,481 --> 00:51:25,292
- [Crow] Laser Gun, starring Pat Carroll.

1300
00:51:25,292 --> 00:51:27,709
(explosions)

1301
00:51:28,815 --> 00:51:30,596
- [Tom] Uh, could someone explain to me

1302
00:51:30,596 --> 00:51:31,897
what's going on here, please?

1303
00:51:31,897 --> 00:51:34,052
- [Joel] It makes no sense.

1304
00:51:34,052 --> 00:51:34,904
- [Tom] Absurd.

1305
00:51:34,904 --> 00:51:37,049
- Eddie, Yuri, are you all right?

1306
00:51:37,049 --> 00:51:37,882
Answer!

1307
00:51:37,882 --> 00:51:41,145
- [Joel] Please phrase it in
the form of a question, sir!

1308
00:51:41,145 --> 00:51:42,628
- We're going after them, get ready.

1309
00:51:42,628 --> 00:51:43,801
- Yes sir!

1310
00:51:43,801 --> 00:51:46,200
- Mary, radio headquarters.
- [Mary] Yes sir!

1311
00:51:46,200 --> 00:51:47,759
- Doctor Hyde, you take over.
- [Doctor] Yes sir.

1312
00:51:47,759 --> 00:51:51,926
- [Tom] It's Mr. Hyde, sir.
(Tom chuckles)

1313
00:51:54,905 --> 00:51:57,322
(blubbering)

1314
00:52:00,868 --> 00:52:02,382
- [Crow] Oh wow, look, it's a way cool

1315
00:52:02,382 --> 00:52:04,938
kinda scary jello thing...

1316
00:52:04,938 --> 00:52:06,877
- What was the research
agency's conclusion?

1317
00:52:06,877 --> 00:52:08,317
- I don't know, they haven't announced it.

1318
00:52:08,317 --> 00:52:09,533
- [Joel] It's Imelda Marcos!

1319
00:52:09,533 --> 00:52:11,037
- But there's one thing
that bothers me, sir.

1320
00:52:11,037 --> 00:52:12,573
- [Tom] My Sgt. Pepper outfit.

1321
00:52:12,573 --> 00:52:15,111
- There was a strange
cargo ship in the harbor.

1322
00:52:15,111 --> 00:52:18,592
I had the feeling that it was
spying on our installations.

1323
00:52:18,592 --> 00:52:20,918
I tried to get its nationality,

1324
00:52:20,918 --> 00:52:23,470
but then it vanished suddenly.

1325
00:52:23,470 --> 00:52:24,581
- Would you recognize it again?

1326
00:52:24,581 --> 00:52:25,414
- Yes.

1327
00:52:25,414 --> 00:52:26,838
- [Crow] Could you pick
it out of a lineup?

1328
00:52:26,838 --> 00:52:28,822
- Well then, I think you ought
to do a little sightseeing

1329
00:52:28,822 --> 00:52:30,518
along the docks.
- [Katherine] Yes sir.

1330
00:52:30,518 --> 00:52:32,963
- [Tom] Say!
- [Joel] Yes sir!

1331
00:52:32,963 --> 00:52:35,788
- Here is that report from
the Technical Research Agency.

1332
00:52:35,788 --> 00:52:38,070
- [Tom] Oh hey look, it's
the old druggy guy again!

1333
00:52:38,070 --> 00:52:41,903
- They believe the island had no density.

1334
00:52:41,903 --> 00:52:44,395
It was only H2O.

1335
00:52:44,395 --> 00:52:47,204
That means, no mass of land,
merely solidified water.

1336
00:52:47,204 --> 00:52:48,612
- [All] You mean ice?

1337
00:52:48,612 --> 00:52:50,916
- Then it should be
floating on the surface,

1338
00:52:50,916 --> 00:52:52,314
because of the specific gravity.

1339
00:52:52,314 --> 00:52:53,615
- [Crow] Could you be more specific?

1340
00:52:53,615 --> 00:52:55,064
- I can't believe it
could sink to the bottom

1341
00:52:55,064 --> 00:52:57,683
of the ocean without
melting in the warm water.

1342
00:52:57,683 --> 00:52:59,496
It's against all the laws of physics.

1343
00:52:59,496 --> 00:53:00,680
- [Tom] Yeah, but can we make it stick?

1344
00:53:00,680 --> 00:53:01,715
Can the DA make a case?

1345
00:53:01,715 --> 00:53:03,336
- One thing is certain, to melt the ice,

1346
00:53:03,336 --> 00:53:05,778
they required intense heat.

1347
00:53:05,778 --> 00:53:07,763
Or there's another possibility.

1348
00:53:07,763 --> 00:53:10,483
Q has found a way to
convert molecular energy.

1349
00:53:10,483 --> 00:53:12,773
- [Joel] Those stinkers!

1350
00:53:12,773 --> 00:53:14,995
- [Yabuki] Various scientists
have been working on it,

1351
00:53:14,995 --> 00:53:16,935
but Q may have found a solution.

1352
00:53:16,935 --> 00:53:17,864
- [Tom] Q's on first.

1353
00:53:17,864 --> 00:53:19,016
- [Crow] That's what I'm asking!

1354
00:53:19,016 --> 00:53:20,360
- [Tom] Third base!

1355
00:53:20,360 --> 00:53:23,187
- If such an important
scientific discovery

1356
00:53:23,187 --> 00:53:26,141
were used only to serve evil purposes.

1357
00:53:26,141 --> 00:53:29,395
Q is powerful, they may
have been able to infiltrate

1358
00:53:29,395 --> 00:53:31,867
our own research center.
- [Joel] Duck.

1359
00:53:31,867 --> 00:53:33,484
- Or maybe they have been able to--

1360
00:53:33,484 --> 00:53:34,567
- [All] Duck.

1361
00:53:35,466 --> 00:53:37,139
- [Joel] Goose!
- [Tom] Run!

1362
00:53:37,139 --> 00:53:39,642
- [Crow] Nice counter blocking, Dad.

1363
00:53:39,642 --> 00:53:43,029
- [Yabuki] Well, principally,
Dr. Takibana of Japan.

1364
00:53:43,029 --> 00:53:45,403
- [Joel] I think the
cameraman's kinda lost interest

1365
00:53:45,403 --> 00:53:48,339
in what's going on in there.

1366
00:53:48,339 --> 00:53:51,185
- [Tom] Wallpaper theater
will be back right after this.

1367
00:53:51,185 --> 00:53:53,350
- [Crow] Nice pattern.

1368
00:53:53,350 --> 00:53:55,803
- [Katherine] Could they
have some connection with Q?

1369
00:53:55,803 --> 00:53:57,190
Could they be agents for the organization?

1370
00:53:57,190 --> 00:53:58,257
- [Crow] Hey, they're talking about us.

1371
00:53:58,257 --> 00:54:00,145
I love when they talk about us!

1372
00:54:00,145 --> 00:54:01,937
- [Yabuki] To investigate
the matter for us, but they--

1373
00:54:01,937 --> 00:54:03,195
- [Tom] Hey.

1374
00:54:03,195 --> 00:54:05,712
Now that is a swell blaupunkt.

1375
00:54:05,712 --> 00:54:08,212
- [Crow] In-dash reel-to-reel.

1376
00:54:10,407 --> 00:54:13,157
- Have you got their photographs?

1377
00:54:14,017 --> 00:54:15,915
- [Joel] Got any wallets?

1378
00:54:15,915 --> 00:54:19,137
- [Yabuki] Here you are.
- Thank you.

1379
00:54:19,137 --> 00:54:22,887
- [Tom] It's Charles
Durning and Walt Disney!

1380
00:54:24,502 --> 00:54:27,956
(Crow clears throat)
- [Crow] What, what?

1381
00:54:27,956 --> 00:54:30,049
- [Joel] Oh, cherry car man.

1382
00:54:30,049 --> 00:54:31,809
Glass packs and thrush pipes.

1383
00:54:31,809 --> 00:54:34,809
(car vocalizations)

1384
00:54:36,948 --> 00:54:40,128
- [Crow] This is CNN!
(ominous music)

1385
00:54:40,128 --> 00:54:42,697
- [Tom] Planned Parenthood?

1386
00:54:42,697 --> 00:54:44,987
- [Joel] Stop the kettle drum!

1387
00:54:44,987 --> 00:54:46,704
(Crow meows)

1388
00:54:46,704 --> 00:54:48,409
- [Villain] Come in, gentlemen, come in.

1389
00:54:48,409 --> 00:54:49,659
- [Joel] Kitty!

1390
00:54:51,556 --> 00:54:52,624
- [Villain] We are now entering

1391
00:54:52,624 --> 00:54:55,013
the final phase of our operation!

1392
00:54:55,013 --> 00:54:56,507
The time has come for us to use

1393
00:54:56,507 --> 00:54:58,756
all the means at our disposal.

1394
00:54:58,756 --> 00:55:00,581
- [Crow] Even you, the Ritz brothers!

1395
00:55:00,581 --> 00:55:02,575
- [Villain] And especially Mighty Jack!

1396
00:55:02,575 --> 00:55:04,366
They have annoyed us too long.

1397
00:55:04,366 --> 00:55:08,548
I wish you every success
in this, our last combat.

1398
00:55:08,548 --> 00:55:10,415
(Tom chuckles)
Good luck gentlemen.

1399
00:55:10,415 --> 00:55:11,576
- [Crow] Manny, moe, Jack.

1400
00:55:11,576 --> 00:55:13,027
- [Villain] Now, you may go.

1401
00:55:13,027 --> 00:55:15,110
- [Three men] Yes master.

1402
00:55:17,227 --> 00:55:19,508
(laughing)

1403
00:55:19,508 --> 00:55:23,258
- [Crow] Hmm, why didn't
they call me master?

1404
00:55:24,882 --> 00:55:26,548
- [Tom] Ooh.

1405
00:55:26,548 --> 00:55:28,048
On the waterfront.

1406
00:55:30,548 --> 00:55:32,039
Oh wow, she's got no toes!

1407
00:55:32,039 --> 00:55:33,122
Foot binding!

1408
00:55:36,308 --> 00:55:38,580
- [Crow] What, is she a merchant
marine all of the sudden?

1409
00:55:38,580 --> 00:55:39,955
Aquamarine, that's the color.

1410
00:55:39,955 --> 00:55:43,006
- [Joel] Oh, my aching imperialist dogs.

1411
00:55:43,006 --> 00:55:47,173
(humming)
(gasps)

1412
00:55:51,106 --> 00:55:55,443
- [Crow] All right lady,
which detergent do you prefer?

1413
00:55:55,443 --> 00:55:56,610
- [Tom] Akiba!

1414
00:55:57,757 --> 00:55:59,325
Woah!

1415
00:55:59,325 --> 00:56:03,492
She is a lean, mean, lime-green
fightin' machine here!

1416
00:56:04,445 --> 00:56:05,875
Good job.

1417
00:56:05,875 --> 00:56:07,954
Oh wait wait wait, two on one?

1418
00:56:07,954 --> 00:56:08,787
- [All] Hey!

1419
00:56:08,787 --> 00:56:10,237
- [Joel] Come on!

1420
00:56:10,237 --> 00:56:11,154
- [Tom] Oh.

1421
00:56:12,353 --> 00:56:13,436
Uncalled for.

1422
00:56:15,025 --> 00:56:16,028
- [Man] Hold it right there!

1423
00:56:16,028 --> 00:56:17,030
- [Joel] Ricky Ricardo?

1424
00:56:17,030 --> 00:56:18,528
- [Crow] Ah Ricky, they're beating me up

1425
00:56:18,528 --> 00:56:21,861
for messing up in the chocolate factory!

1426
00:56:23,000 --> 00:56:25,250
(grunting)

1427
00:56:26,243 --> 00:56:27,672
- [Man] Come with me.

1428
00:56:27,672 --> 00:56:29,795
(gentle music)

1429
00:56:29,795 --> 00:56:33,634
- [Crow] Hey, she's been
kidnapped by the Partridge Family!

1430
00:56:33,634 --> 00:56:37,717
- [Joel] And they're
playing Echo Valley 6080209.

1431
00:56:41,078 --> 00:56:44,161
(singing in Spanish)

1432
00:56:48,074 --> 00:56:50,422
- Oh, you're back with us again.

1433
00:56:50,422 --> 00:56:51,361
- [Katherine] Where am I?

1434
00:56:51,361 --> 00:56:52,961
- A bus I requisitioned.

1435
00:56:52,961 --> 00:56:54,369
- [Tom] My name is Bobby Zimmerman.

1436
00:56:54,369 --> 00:56:55,681
- Cozy isn't it?

1437
00:56:55,681 --> 00:56:57,910
Have you any idea what they wanted?

1438
00:56:57,910 --> 00:57:00,673
- No, I have no idea at all.

1439
00:57:00,673 --> 00:57:03,116
Maybe they were after my money?

1440
00:57:03,116 --> 00:57:04,897
Thank you for rescuing me.

1441
00:57:04,897 --> 00:57:07,073
- Nothing, don't even mention it.

1442
00:57:07,073 --> 00:57:08,406
- [Tom] Okay.
- [Katherine] Oh!

1443
00:57:08,406 --> 00:57:10,796
- Something annoying you?
- [Tom] Yeah, your capo.

1444
00:57:10,796 --> 00:57:13,376
- You're Manuel Perez!
- [Crow] No, I'm Sancho Panza.

1445
00:57:13,376 --> 00:57:16,341
- I recognize you,
aren't you Manuel Perez?

1446
00:57:16,341 --> 00:57:18,198
- [Crow] Oui, I am that person.

1447
00:57:18,198 --> 00:57:21,517
- You've always been a hero figure to me.

1448
00:57:21,517 --> 00:57:23,233
I've read your books and know all about

1449
00:57:23,233 --> 00:57:24,993
your early struggles.
- [Tom] Say.

1450
00:57:24,993 --> 00:57:27,585
- [Katherine] You did such
good work in the third world.

1451
00:57:27,585 --> 00:57:29,462
- [Joel] Oh, are you speaking to me?

1452
00:57:29,462 --> 00:57:30,379
Oh, I see.

1453
00:57:30,379 --> 00:57:34,555
- [Katharine] Are you
still involved in politics?

1454
00:57:34,555 --> 00:57:37,171
- [Tom] Woah, the politics of motion.

1455
00:57:37,171 --> 00:57:38,291
(wolf whistle)

1456
00:57:38,291 --> 00:57:39,953
- [Joel] The politics of feeling good.

1457
00:57:39,953 --> 00:57:42,370
Ah, we'll order off the menu.

1458
00:57:43,586 --> 00:57:44,782
- [Crow] Oh man, look
at the appendix scar,

1459
00:57:44,782 --> 00:57:46,403
who's the body double, Jack Klugman?

1460
00:57:46,403 --> 00:57:47,403
- [Tom] Yow!

1461
00:57:49,209 --> 00:57:51,790
- [Joel] Ah, we're
trying to eat over here!

1462
00:57:51,790 --> 00:57:54,489
- [Crow] I love going to Fridays.

1463
00:57:54,489 --> 00:57:56,003
- Salud.

1464
00:57:56,003 --> 00:57:57,475
- [Joel] I was in Anna
Christie at the Provencetown--

1465
00:57:57,475 --> 00:57:58,691
- [Tom] Thank you!

1466
00:57:58,691 --> 00:58:01,191
(jazzy music)

1467
00:58:03,374 --> 00:58:05,724
- Excuse me a second.

1468
00:58:05,724 --> 00:58:08,318
Look after him.
- [Woman] Sure.

1469
00:58:08,318 --> 00:58:11,817
- [Tom] She's going to throw up.

1470
00:58:11,817 --> 00:58:12,883
- What took you so long?

1471
00:58:12,883 --> 00:58:14,409
I was beginning to get worried.

1472
00:58:14,409 --> 00:58:16,391
Was that the ship?
- [Katherine] No.

1473
00:58:16,391 --> 00:58:17,971
But something else happened.

1474
00:58:17,971 --> 00:58:20,170
Q tried to kidnap me.

1475
00:58:20,170 --> 00:58:22,396
Only I was saved, by this man, Perez.

1476
00:58:22,396 --> 00:58:24,603
- [Tom] Did he give you those jammies?

1477
00:58:24,603 --> 00:58:26,365
- [Crow] Hey, a View-Master!

1478
00:58:26,365 --> 00:58:28,365
And it's Mount Rushmore!

1479
00:58:33,966 --> 00:58:36,299
- [Joel] It's Mel Torme!
- [Tom] It's Don Adams!

1480
00:58:36,299 --> 00:58:38,607
- [Joel] Noel Coward?
- [Crow] Tommy Sledge?

1481
00:58:38,607 --> 00:58:40,563
- Oh, can I help you?

1482
00:58:40,563 --> 00:58:42,109
Are you looking for anything special?

1483
00:58:42,109 --> 00:58:44,339
- Oh no, I'm just browsing around.

1484
00:58:44,339 --> 00:58:46,888
You see, I have to do a lot of travelling,

1485
00:58:46,888 --> 00:58:49,288
so I'm always buying travel guides.

1486
00:58:49,288 --> 00:58:50,589
- [Tom] That's a picture of you naked!

1487
00:58:50,589 --> 00:58:52,157
You are sick!

1488
00:58:52,157 --> 00:58:55,026
- Special correspondent
for World Magazine,

1489
00:58:55,026 --> 00:58:56,359
Roberto Okamura.

1490
00:58:57,437 --> 00:58:58,760
Well!

1491
00:58:58,760 --> 00:59:00,242
You're the famous writer, aren't you?

1492
00:59:00,242 --> 00:59:02,845
- [Joel] Well, could be, your
guess is as good as mine.

1493
00:59:02,845 --> 00:59:05,085
- I read one of your
articles a short while ago.

1494
00:59:05,085 --> 00:59:05,918
- [Crow] It sucked!

1495
00:59:05,918 --> 00:59:07,464
- And I thought you did a
wonderful job describing

1496
00:59:07,464 --> 00:59:10,161
Q's increasing power in
the various countries.

1497
00:59:10,161 --> 00:59:11,475
- [Tom] Oui, I did do that.

1498
00:59:11,475 --> 00:59:14,419
- You have a rather
special interest in it.

1499
00:59:14,419 --> 00:59:16,573
Mighty Jack interests you too, I guess?

1500
00:59:16,573 --> 00:59:19,473
(crosstalk)
(whistling)

1501
00:59:19,473 --> 00:59:21,308
- Oh, I don't know what you mean.

1502
00:59:21,308 --> 00:59:23,324
I'm only a salesgirl in this store here.

1503
00:59:23,324 --> 00:59:24,847
- [Crow] I'm not an
operative for Mighty Jack.

1504
00:59:24,847 --> 00:59:28,200
- Why don't we step out and
have a little cup of coffee?

1505
00:59:28,200 --> 00:59:29,793
Just the two of us.

1506
00:59:29,793 --> 00:59:31,563
- [Joel] Building castles in the sand.

1507
00:59:31,563 --> 00:59:32,950
- About Mighty Jack.

1508
00:59:32,950 --> 00:59:35,358
It's got a lot of friends in this store.

1509
00:59:35,358 --> 00:59:36,191
- Roberto.

1510
00:59:37,121 --> 00:59:39,115
I don't think that your readers

1511
00:59:39,115 --> 00:59:41,451
would be interested in
what goes on around here.

1512
00:59:41,451 --> 00:59:42,518
Do you?

1513
00:59:42,518 --> 00:59:46,175
- Ah, you're the person in
charge here, Mr. Atari, right?

1514
00:59:46,175 --> 00:59:48,513
- [Tom] Still trying to launch Pong, eh?

1515
00:59:48,513 --> 00:59:50,486
- Yes, the famous Mr. Atari.

1516
00:59:50,486 --> 00:59:51,499
(laughing)

1517
00:59:51,499 --> 00:59:53,857
You know what puzzles me?

1518
00:59:53,857 --> 00:59:56,095
The newspapers often
talk about Mighty Jack.

1519
00:59:56,095 --> 00:59:57,793
- [Crow] But nobody
does anything about it!

1520
00:59:57,793 --> 00:59:59,668
- They never mention the crew.

1521
00:59:59,668 --> 01:00:01,289
Not once.

1522
01:00:01,289 --> 01:00:03,062
Only the mechanical details.

1523
01:00:03,062 --> 01:00:05,918
The design and all its latest equipment.

1524
01:00:05,918 --> 01:00:08,705
I have a responsibility to our readers.

1525
01:00:08,705 --> 01:00:11,173
I'd like to write about who the crew is.

1526
01:00:11,173 --> 01:00:13,393
All human interest stuff, you know.

1527
01:00:13,393 --> 01:00:16,614
- Well, then write what you have to.

1528
01:00:16,614 --> 01:00:19,622
- [Crow] Uh-oh.
(screaming)

1529
01:00:19,622 --> 01:00:22,455
- [Tom] Oh, I forgot it's Tuesday!

1530
01:00:23,467 --> 01:00:24,768
- Are you all right, Roberto?

1531
01:00:24,768 --> 01:00:26,966
- [Crow] No, my elbow
exploded, what do you think?

1532
01:00:26,966 --> 01:00:29,525
(ominous music)

1533
01:00:29,525 --> 01:00:31,692
Oswald.
- [Tom] No, no, no.

1534
01:00:33,341 --> 01:00:37,053
Hey, don't point, that's not polite.

1535
01:00:37,053 --> 01:00:39,803
- [Crow] Wait, Mr. Ice Cream man!

1536
01:00:41,277 --> 01:00:42,728
- Up there, the roof!

1537
01:00:42,728 --> 01:00:45,622
- [Joel] Up yours, you goof!

1538
01:00:45,622 --> 01:00:47,622
- [Crow] Kato, look out!

1539
01:00:52,785 --> 01:00:53,948
- Blasted!

1540
01:00:53,948 --> 01:00:56,241
- [Tom] Targermagarget!

1541
01:00:56,241 --> 01:00:57,415
- Jerry!
- [Crow] Dean!

1542
01:00:57,415 --> 01:00:59,377
- Where is he?
- [Jerry] He got away!

1543
01:00:59,377 --> 01:01:00,572
- Oh, what have you got there?

1544
01:01:00,572 --> 01:01:02,163
- [Tom] Wait, he's talking to himself.

1545
01:01:02,163 --> 01:01:03,496
What's goin' on?

1546
01:01:05,301 --> 01:01:07,340
- [Joel] Your wind song stays on my mind.

1547
01:01:07,340 --> 01:01:10,199
- Strange-looking
bullet, it's transparent.

1548
01:01:10,199 --> 01:01:11,873
- [Crow] Like this plot.

1549
01:01:11,873 --> 01:01:15,649
- [Jerry] I've never seen
anything like this before.

1550
01:01:15,649 --> 01:01:17,772
- [Tom] Hello.
- [Yabuki] How did it go?

1551
01:01:17,772 --> 01:01:19,255
- [Atari] Same results as before.

1552
01:01:19,255 --> 01:01:20,833
- Is that so?

1553
01:01:20,833 --> 01:01:23,831
- We raised the heat to 800
degrees without melting it.

1554
01:01:23,831 --> 01:01:26,327
Or even altering its molecular structure.

1555
01:01:26,327 --> 01:01:28,439
It's definite proof that--
- [Tom] Shh!

1556
01:01:28,439 --> 01:01:30,689
The man might be listening.

1557
01:01:34,295 --> 01:01:35,128
Ah!

1558
01:01:36,951 --> 01:01:37,951
- [Crow] Oh.

1559
01:01:39,628 --> 01:01:41,878
(grunting)

1560
01:01:43,063 --> 01:01:44,236
Rolling papers.

1561
01:01:44,236 --> 01:01:47,574
I'll roll us a doob, you
put on some Allman Brothers.

1562
01:01:47,574 --> 01:01:52,492
That Eat a Peach album.
(chuckling)

1563
01:01:52,492 --> 01:01:53,575
(blubbering)

1564
01:01:53,575 --> 01:01:57,108
- [Joel] It's a wonderful
afternoon to be doing--

1565
01:01:57,108 --> 01:01:58,110
- You knew about that?

1566
01:01:58,110 --> 01:02:02,074
- Sometimes its necessary to
keep the enemy well informed.

1567
01:02:02,074 --> 01:02:03,358
- I thought that we ought to tell them

1568
01:02:03,358 --> 01:02:05,854
we knew about the high-temperature ice.

1569
01:02:05,854 --> 01:02:07,988
Now we'll wait and see how they react.

1570
01:02:07,988 --> 01:02:08,821
- Oh.

1571
01:02:10,046 --> 01:02:12,190
You mean Roberto?
- [Tom] Duran?

1572
01:02:12,190 --> 01:02:14,590
- Yes, he's an agent of Q.

1573
01:02:14,590 --> 01:02:15,881
- And Perez?

1574
01:02:15,881 --> 01:02:17,097
- [Crow] Well, we'll always have Paris.

1575
01:02:17,097 --> 01:02:18,206
- There's no proof yet.

1576
01:02:18,206 --> 01:02:20,425
Katherine's investigating that now.

1577
01:02:20,425 --> 01:02:23,932
- I understand Dr. Takibana
will be returning tomorrow.

1578
01:02:23,932 --> 01:02:26,078
- [Atari] Good, we'll go question him.

1579
01:02:26,078 --> 01:02:27,273
- [Jerry] Is the doctor a Q agent?

1580
01:02:27,273 --> 01:02:28,969
- [Joel] Is the doctor a Q agent?

1581
01:02:28,969 --> 01:02:30,334
(mocking vocalizations)

1582
01:02:30,334 --> 01:02:31,715
- [Yabuki] A job for you, Atari.

1583
01:02:31,715 --> 01:02:32,548
- Yes.

1584
01:02:35,491 --> 01:02:39,241
- [Tom] On a very special
Trapper John, MD...

1585
01:02:40,910 --> 01:02:43,065
- [Crow] Oh, it's thirsty
Thursday, two bucks for a mug,

1586
01:02:43,065 --> 01:02:45,465
and then raspberry comets
are a buck after that.

1587
01:02:45,465 --> 01:02:46,457
- [Tom] Wow.
- [Crow] Yeah.

1588
01:02:46,457 --> 01:02:47,406
- Interesting lecture.

1589
01:02:47,406 --> 01:02:48,515
- Yes, I enjoyed it.

1590
01:02:48,515 --> 01:02:50,478
(murmuring)

1591
01:02:50,478 --> 01:02:52,249
- [Tom] So he's liquid metal, eh?

1592
01:02:52,249 --> 01:02:53,753
- Excuse me doctors, we'd
like to speak to you.

1593
01:02:53,753 --> 01:02:56,089
- Not now, I'm very busy.
- [Atari] It's about hot ice.

1594
01:02:56,089 --> 01:02:57,155
(gasping)

1595
01:02:57,155 --> 01:02:59,896
- [Tom] Wow, my favorite band!

1596
01:02:59,896 --> 01:03:00,729
- Here.

1597
01:03:06,446 --> 01:03:09,038
It's not made of glass, but only of water.

1598
01:03:09,038 --> 01:03:10,926
- [Crow] But it's the best I can do.

1599
01:03:10,926 --> 01:03:12,489
- [Atari] I believe you were
working on this experiment.

1600
01:03:12,489 --> 01:03:13,343
(sniffing)

1601
01:03:13,343 --> 01:03:16,495
- [Tom] Did you clean that off real good?

1602
01:03:16,495 --> 01:03:17,745
Ice, ice, baby?

1603
01:03:20,353 --> 01:03:23,127
- Would you gentlemen excuse me?

1604
01:03:23,127 --> 01:03:25,460
(crosstalk)

1605
01:03:26,380 --> 01:03:27,213
Thank you.

1606
01:03:28,232 --> 01:03:30,952
Oh, Fritz, I'll take that.

1607
01:03:30,952 --> 01:03:33,232
- [Tom] Sure thing, stach.

1608
01:03:33,232 --> 01:03:36,075
- This is Fritz, he's my assistant.

1609
01:03:36,075 --> 01:03:38,377
- Atari
- [Fritz] How do you do?

1610
01:03:38,377 --> 01:03:41,168
- Jerry.
- [Fritz] How do you do?

1611
01:03:41,168 --> 01:03:42,768
Well, I must go now.

1612
01:03:42,768 --> 01:03:44,742
- Goodbye.
- [Tom] Okay, goodbye.

1613
01:03:44,742 --> 01:03:45,648
- Shall we go to my office?

1614
01:03:45,648 --> 01:03:48,231
(upbeat music)

1615
01:03:52,960 --> 01:03:55,327
- Someone broke in and
stole all my records.

1616
01:03:55,327 --> 01:03:56,982
[Crosstalk]

1617
01:03:56,982 --> 01:03:57,935
10 years of research.
- [Tom] Bummer.

1618
01:03:57,935 --> 01:04:00,368
- I'd nearly completed all my experiments.

1619
01:04:00,368 --> 01:04:03,219
And then, one day all my papers were gone.

1620
01:04:03,219 --> 01:04:04,744
- [Tom] So I quit my route.

1621
01:04:04,744 --> 01:04:07,507
- [Takibana] What a tragedy.
- [Tom] Liberty, egality.

1622
01:04:07,507 --> 01:04:09,544
- And now I see that someone has

1623
01:04:09,544 --> 01:04:12,925
carried my work to its final stage.

1624
01:04:12,925 --> 01:04:15,549
Ice that won't melt, even
under very high temperatures.

1625
01:04:15,549 --> 01:04:16,850
- [All] So what?

1626
01:04:16,850 --> 01:04:20,520
- Atari, have you any idea
who could've stolen them?

1627
01:04:20,520 --> 01:04:22,451
- Could it be Dr. Funmueller
from West Germany?

1628
01:04:22,451 --> 01:04:24,392
- [Tom] Wrong, go fish!

1629
01:04:24,392 --> 01:04:26,429
- He's engaged in similar research,

1630
01:04:26,429 --> 01:04:29,276
though our methods are quite different.

1631
01:04:29,276 --> 01:04:31,614
If you analyze this substance,

1632
01:04:31,614 --> 01:04:32,978
you will see that it could not

1633
01:04:32,978 --> 01:04:34,925
have been made without using my process.

1634
01:04:34,925 --> 01:04:36,215
- [Crow] With liquid metal.

1635
01:04:36,215 --> 01:04:38,594
- Fritz, your assistant?

1636
01:04:38,594 --> 01:04:40,717
- [Takibana] No, definitely not.

1637
01:04:40,717 --> 01:04:41,837
- Why not?

1638
01:04:41,837 --> 01:04:44,246
- You see, Fritz is my son.
(Crow gasps)

1639
01:04:44,246 --> 01:04:46,461
- [Tom] You named your son Fritz?

1640
01:04:46,461 --> 01:04:49,853
- [Takibana] My wife died many
years ago, she was German.

1641
01:04:49,853 --> 01:04:51,709
- [Tom] So you're available?
- [Takibana] Fritz is my son.

1642
01:04:51,709 --> 01:04:53,960
He grew up in Berlin.

1643
01:04:53,960 --> 01:04:55,261
- I understand.

1644
01:04:55,261 --> 01:04:56,870
- Atari.

1645
01:04:56,870 --> 01:04:59,603
I told you a little while ago

1646
01:04:59,603 --> 01:05:02,353
all that work of 10 years had been stolen.

1647
01:05:02,353 --> 01:05:04,155
- [Crow] I lied.

1648
01:05:04,155 --> 01:05:06,451
- It was a great loss.

1649
01:05:06,451 --> 01:05:08,540
But now I realize I was
wrong to speak about

1650
01:05:08,540 --> 01:05:11,997
my work prematurely.
- [Joel] Oops.

1651
01:05:11,997 --> 01:05:14,736
- It was out of vanity.
- [Joel] And Apollonia.

1652
01:05:14,736 --> 01:05:17,569
- I opened the door for the thief.

1653
01:05:18,653 --> 01:05:21,320
(ominous music)

1654
01:05:23,740 --> 01:05:24,584
- What do you think?

1655
01:05:24,584 --> 01:05:25,715
- [Crow] Let's go Italian today.

1656
01:05:25,715 --> 01:05:27,901
- It's hard to say if
he's telling the truth.

1657
01:05:27,901 --> 01:05:29,693
But he sounded very sincere.

1658
01:05:29,693 --> 01:05:32,583
- There's still one suspect.
- [Jerry] Who?

1659
01:05:32,583 --> 01:05:33,949
- Dr. Funmueller.

1660
01:05:33,949 --> 01:05:35,731
- [Tom] Oh, the Chinese guy!

1661
01:05:35,731 --> 01:05:37,064
- Let's go then.

1662
01:05:39,240 --> 01:05:42,951
- [Crow] Mystery guest, sign in please!

1663
01:05:42,951 --> 01:05:46,131
Well here we are at Doctor
Klutzy Von Doorknob's place.

1664
01:05:46,131 --> 01:05:48,893
- Well, Atari, it's good you're here.

1665
01:05:48,893 --> 01:05:50,963
I'd like to introduce
this gentleman to you.

1666
01:05:50,963 --> 01:05:52,115
This is Dr. Funmueller.

1667
01:05:52,115 --> 01:05:53,331
- [Tom] We've been smoking Lebanese Blonde

1668
01:05:53,331 --> 01:05:54,941
and we're flying right now.

1669
01:05:54,941 --> 01:05:56,781
- How do you do?
- [Atari] Doctor.

1670
01:05:56,781 --> 01:05:59,331
(buzzing)
- [Crow] Joy buzzer.

1671
01:05:59,331 --> 01:06:00,831
Oh, love that gag.

1672
01:06:04,131 --> 01:06:06,296
- Atari.
- [Atari] Sir?

1673
01:06:06,296 --> 01:06:07,645
- [Tom] Where do you get your seat waxed?

1674
01:06:07,645 --> 01:06:10,525
- Claims that all his research
documents have been stolen.

1675
01:06:10,525 --> 01:06:14,744
- [Crow] Oh Andy, oh my
research documents, oh.

1676
01:06:14,744 --> 01:06:16,157
- Ja.

1677
01:06:16,157 --> 01:06:18,557
- Then you're half Japanese, half French,

1678
01:06:18,557 --> 01:06:20,690
with some Vietnamese
mixed in, is that right?

1679
01:06:20,690 --> 01:06:22,524
- [Joel] Yeah, the call me mongrel boy.

1680
01:06:22,524 --> 01:06:25,613
- During the war, I was
sent to school in Italy.

1681
01:06:25,613 --> 01:06:29,780
- [Tom] 3/16ths speed,
that's all I ever heard.

1682
01:06:30,838 --> 01:06:33,976
- I never saw either of them again.

1683
01:06:33,976 --> 01:06:35,821
They both died in Vietnam.

1684
01:06:35,821 --> 01:06:36,907
- [Crow] Oh, that war.

1685
01:06:36,907 --> 01:06:38,690
Shh, don't talk about that war.

1686
01:06:38,690 --> 01:06:40,205
- [Joel] No.

1687
01:06:40,205 --> 01:06:42,626
- I'm sure you suffered a great deal then.

1688
01:06:42,626 --> 01:06:43,974
- [Crow] Suffered, oh yes, yes.

1689
01:06:43,974 --> 01:06:45,828
- But today, the world's
a different place.

1690
01:06:45,828 --> 01:06:48,271
There's so much to live for!

1691
01:06:48,271 --> 01:06:51,451
- [Joel] Oh, you don't
know the half of it.

1692
01:06:51,451 --> 01:06:55,323
- They say that the happiest
people are the ones with faith.

1693
01:06:55,323 --> 01:06:59,490
- [Tom] What are ya, Barbra
Streisand all of the sudden?

1694
01:07:01,136 --> 01:07:02,747
- Oh.

1695
01:07:02,747 --> 01:07:05,200
I'm afraid that I left
my cigarette lighter

1696
01:07:05,200 --> 01:07:06,683
in your store the other day.

1697
01:07:06,683 --> 01:07:07,718
(Tom chuckles)

1698
01:07:07,718 --> 01:07:10,330
- The one who stole those
papers must be working for Q.

1699
01:07:10,330 --> 01:07:12,112
We have to try and set some kind of trap

1700
01:07:12,112 --> 01:07:14,395
to discover the traitor, right?

1701
01:07:14,395 --> 01:07:15,840
Harry, Eddy?
- [Both] Yes sir?

1702
01:07:15,840 --> 01:07:17,867
- Find out who else had
access to those files.

1703
01:07:17,867 --> 01:07:19,488
- [Crow] Hey, what's William
Faulkner doing in there?

1704
01:07:19,488 --> 01:07:20,566
- Did you see a lighter?

1705
01:07:20,566 --> 01:07:21,878
- [Joel] Hey, that scene just hooked up

1706
01:07:21,878 --> 01:07:23,360
with the other scene...
- [Tom] Wow!

1707
01:07:23,360 --> 01:07:25,752
- [Joel] Oh, now they're back.

1708
01:07:25,752 --> 01:07:26,902
- Thank you.

1709
01:07:26,902 --> 01:07:29,248
And here's something for you.

1710
01:07:29,248 --> 01:07:30,356
- Oh.

1711
01:07:30,356 --> 01:07:32,703
- Well, it's been real nice.

1712
01:07:32,703 --> 01:07:34,219
- [Tom] See ya later kid.

1713
01:07:34,219 --> 01:07:35,755
♫ Dooby dooby doo ♫

1714
01:07:35,755 --> 01:07:38,172
(vocalizing)

1715
01:07:41,364 --> 01:07:43,200
- [Crow] Ah, Rupert Murdoch.

1716
01:07:43,200 --> 01:07:45,867
(all whistling)

1717
01:07:51,990 --> 01:07:53,419
- [Joel] Enough.

1718
01:07:53,419 --> 01:07:54,784
- [Crow] Now we have to
pay the French government.

1719
01:07:54,784 --> 01:07:56,726
- [Joel] Oh, this is
just like the chase scene

1720
01:07:56,726 --> 01:07:58,539
from the French Connection.

1721
01:07:58,539 --> 01:08:00,149
- [Tom] I thought that was French.

1722
01:08:00,149 --> 01:08:02,066
The whole French thing.

1723
01:08:03,115 --> 01:08:04,532
It's very French.

1724
01:08:06,688 --> 01:08:08,000
Oh, they're just going to spend some time

1725
01:08:08,000 --> 01:08:10,333
in the discipline box there.

1726
01:08:12,598 --> 01:08:14,431
- [Jerry] Mighty Jack.

1727
01:08:19,222 --> 01:08:20,715
- Perez.

1728
01:08:20,715 --> 01:08:21,555
Avanti!

1729
01:08:21,555 --> 01:08:22,891
- Si.

1730
01:08:22,891 --> 01:08:23,808
- [Tom] Si?

1731
01:08:27,627 --> 01:08:30,304
- Been waiting long?
- [Crow] All my life.

1732
01:08:30,304 --> 01:08:31,811
- Oh!

1733
01:08:31,811 --> 01:08:32,854
- [Tom] That long huh?

1734
01:08:32,854 --> 01:08:33,908
- I'm going out to eat now.

1735
01:08:33,908 --> 01:08:35,243
I just came into a little money,

1736
01:08:35,243 --> 01:08:36,489
you free for dinner tonight?

1737
01:08:36,489 --> 01:08:39,135
- Yes, I am.
- [Tom] Arby's okay?

1738
01:08:39,135 --> 01:08:40,011
- Is this your car?

1739
01:08:40,011 --> 01:08:41,898
