- [Tom] You're stuck here!

1798
01:10:50,713 --> 01:10:53,977
- Perez, contact our agent right away.

1799
01:10:53,977 --> 01:10:56,847
- [Crow] Get us out of this film.

1800
01:10:56,847 --> 01:10:59,274
- [Tom] It's Woody Guthrie.

1801
01:10:59,274 --> 01:11:01,956
- [Joel] Hey, my mood
ring's going all kooky!

1802
01:11:01,956 --> 01:11:04,181
(beeping)

1803
01:11:04,181 --> 01:11:05,625
- [Crow] Adam West?

1804
01:11:05,625 --> 01:11:06,948
Pete Dupont?

1805
01:11:06,948 --> 01:11:09,698
- [Tom] Yeah, he looks like Pete.

1806
01:11:12,825 --> 01:11:14,148
- [Fritz] Hello father.

1807
01:11:14,148 --> 01:11:15,643
- [Crow] Hello Mother.

1808
01:11:15,643 --> 01:11:17,545
- [Tom] Here I am in Okinawa.

1809
01:11:17,545 --> 01:11:19,956
- So you're the one who--
- [Fritz] Yes.

1810
01:11:19,956 --> 01:11:22,441
You should have realized it long ago.

1811
01:11:22,441 --> 01:11:25,801
I opened your safe and
gave all your records to Q.

1812
01:11:25,801 --> 01:11:26,729
- [Takibana] How could you?

1813
01:11:26,729 --> 01:11:28,340
All my life's work.

1814
01:11:28,340 --> 01:11:29,173
- [Tom] The Archies.

1815
01:11:29,173 --> 01:11:31,576
- [Takibana] You, of
all people, my own son.

1816
01:11:31,576 --> 01:11:33,487
- Yes, I knew you'd say that.

1817
01:11:33,487 --> 01:11:37,028
All my life, you could
only think of me Japanese,

1818
01:11:37,028 --> 01:11:38,393
but inside I'm German.

1819
01:11:38,393 --> 01:11:40,269
- [Joel] Kinda like sushi stroganoff.

1820
01:11:40,269 --> 01:11:41,880
- How much did they give you to betray me

1821
01:11:41,880 --> 01:11:43,686
and work with those monsters?

1822
01:11:43,686 --> 01:11:44,838
- You've never acknowledged--

1823
01:11:44,838 --> 01:11:46,982
- [Crow] Now he looks like Roddy McDowall.

1824
01:11:46,982 --> 01:11:47,972
- [Tom] I don't get it.

1825
01:11:47,972 --> 01:11:50,874
- All those years, you took the credit.

1826
01:11:50,874 --> 01:11:53,423
Only now, things will be different.

1827
01:11:53,423 --> 01:11:55,196
I'll have my own laboratory.

1828
01:11:55,196 --> 01:11:57,626
With Q I have a great future.

1829
01:11:57,626 --> 01:11:59,020
- [Tom] My own room and my own phone too!

1830
01:11:59,020 --> 01:12:00,620
- Stealing another man's ideas?

1831
01:12:00,620 --> 01:12:03,793
- [Tom] Ooh!
- Betraying your father?

1832
01:12:03,793 --> 01:12:05,541
By dealing with murderers?

1833
01:12:05,541 --> 01:12:07,610
- Yes.
- [Tom] Yes!

1834
01:12:07,610 --> 01:12:09,947
- Your ideas and ethics are too antiquated

1835
01:12:09,947 --> 01:12:12,316
for you to understand
what we are creating.

1836
01:12:12,316 --> 01:12:13,990
- [Joel] Look at my
warts, I had to be evil!

1837
01:12:13,990 --> 01:12:16,604
- Conquer the whole world.
(laughing)

1838
01:12:16,604 --> 01:12:17,905
- [Joel] Well, it's good to have goals.

1839
01:12:17,905 --> 01:12:18,738
- Fritz!

1840
01:12:19,622 --> 01:12:20,614
- [Crow] The Wicker Man?

1841
01:12:20,614 --> 01:12:21,702
Now they're in Ireland!

1842
01:12:21,702 --> 01:12:23,654
- Why have we come here?

1843
01:12:23,654 --> 01:12:26,246
- I have proof that Dr.
Takibana was working for Q.

1844
01:12:26,246 --> 01:12:27,324
(Mary and Tom gasp)

1845
01:12:27,324 --> 01:12:29,030
I'm going to check out his apartment.

1846
01:12:29,030 --> 01:12:30,652
You stay as lookout.

1847
01:12:30,652 --> 01:12:31,942
- [Tom] Oh, we can't stay, we gotta go.

1848
01:12:31,942 --> 01:12:32,977
- You stay here!

1849
01:12:32,977 --> 01:12:34,886
(crosstalk)

1850
01:12:34,886 --> 01:12:37,386
- [Joel] We go, you stay here.

1851
01:12:41,300 --> 01:12:43,967
(doors closing)

1852
01:12:49,318 --> 01:12:50,340
- Help, help!

1853
01:12:50,340 --> 01:12:51,772
Watered the ship!

1854
01:12:51,772 --> 01:12:53,265
We're all gonna die!

1855
01:12:53,265 --> 01:12:54,684
A fireball!

1856
01:12:54,684 --> 01:12:56,284
- Joel, come on, you're
not fooling anybody.

1857
01:12:56,284 --> 01:12:58,074
That's an aquarium you
put in front of Cambot

1858
01:12:58,074 --> 01:12:59,418
that's causing this effect here.

1859
01:12:59,418 --> 01:13:00,870
- I know, I know, I was just getting ready

1860
01:13:00,870 --> 01:13:02,257
to do a big pitch to Hollywood.

1861
01:13:02,257 --> 01:13:04,284
You know, we got tons of offers from

1862
01:13:04,284 --> 01:13:07,270
interested executives
after Crow read his piece

1863
01:13:07,270 --> 01:13:09,692
in Reader's Theater
called Earth Versus Soup.

1864
01:13:09,692 --> 01:13:11,430
- Yep, now I've got a development deal

1865
01:13:11,430 --> 01:13:13,723
with Anson Williams'
Enchantment Productions,

1866
01:13:13,723 --> 01:13:16,305
and plus, I'm doing a
rewrite on Next of Kin II.

1867
01:13:16,305 --> 01:13:18,705
- Yeah, so I thought we could
do the pitch underwater.

1868
01:13:18,705 --> 01:13:20,945
You know, like cash in
on some of the excitement

1869
01:13:20,945 --> 01:13:23,462
that's been generated
from movies like The Deep

1870
01:13:23,462 --> 01:13:25,659
and The Abyss and others.

1871
01:13:25,659 --> 01:13:27,121
- Wow, that's a great idea Joel.

1872
01:13:27,121 --> 01:13:28,998
As a matter of fact, I was
just watching Mighty Jack,

1873
01:13:28,998 --> 01:13:30,118
and I couldn't help but think,

1874
01:13:30,118 --> 01:13:31,665
this would make a great movie!

1875
01:13:31,665 --> 01:13:33,585
- Right, yeah, okay.

1876
01:13:33,585 --> 01:13:36,710
I was thinking like started
off with a submarine.

1877
01:13:36,710 --> 01:13:39,548
(vocalizing)

1878
01:13:39,548 --> 01:13:41,756
Grey Lady down Grey Lady down!

1879
01:13:41,756 --> 01:13:43,996
I can't seem him, they got
a caterpillar here, sir!

1880
01:13:43,996 --> 01:13:46,406
- [Tom] Nice Joel, that's nice.

1881
01:13:46,406 --> 01:13:48,482
- [Crow] Ha ha, great Joel.

1882
01:13:48,482 --> 01:13:51,432
The man should be in a straight jacket.

1883
01:13:51,432 --> 01:13:53,272
- [Joel] Here come the
animals, two by two.

1884
01:13:53,272 --> 01:13:54,467
- [Tom] Woah woah, what does Noah

1885
01:13:54,467 --> 01:13:55,949
have to do with anything here Joel?

1886
01:13:55,949 --> 01:13:57,644
- [Joel] It's the ark of
the of the star eater!

1887
01:13:57,644 --> 01:13:59,469
- [Crow] That's it, that's
it, get me around here.

1888
01:13:59,469 --> 01:14:00,824
- [Tom] Go tear his arm off!
- [Joel] Hey wait a minute!

1889
01:14:00,824 --> 01:14:02,147
What are you tryin' to do?

1890
01:14:02,147 --> 01:14:03,832
- [Crow] I was gonna tear your arm off.

1891
01:14:03,832 --> 01:14:04,717
- [Joel] Oh, come on.

1892
01:14:04,717 --> 01:14:07,395
Anyway, the really good thing is that

1893
01:14:07,395 --> 01:14:09,187
Steven Spielberg is now doing a bunch of

1894
01:14:09,187 --> 01:14:11,021
movies based on cartoon characters.

1895
01:14:11,021 --> 01:14:14,189
You know, like the
Flintstones and Bloom County.

1896
01:14:14,189 --> 01:14:16,534
And, it just goes on like that.

1897
01:14:16,534 --> 01:14:17,670
- [Tom] Yeah, what's he gonna do next,

1898
01:14:17,670 --> 01:14:18,840
Casper the Friendly Ghost?
(laughing)

1899
01:14:18,840 --> 01:14:20,104
- [Joel] Oh, don't be ridiculous.

1900
01:14:20,104 --> 01:14:21,843
I was thinking it'd be a great time

1901
01:14:21,843 --> 01:14:24,499
to bring even more cartoon
characters to the big screen.

1902
01:14:24,499 --> 01:14:28,019
You know, like Deputy Dog.
- [Tom] That's Droopy.

1903
01:14:28,019 --> 01:14:30,653
- [Joel] And Otie Calony.

1904
01:14:30,653 --> 01:14:32,018
And Josie and the Pussycats.

1905
01:14:32,018 --> 01:14:33,501
- [Tom] I can't stand to
see him like this Crow.

1906
01:14:33,501 --> 01:14:35,834
- [Crow] No, I can't either.

1907
01:14:37,256 --> 01:14:39,112
- Hey, you guys, come back.

1908
01:14:39,112 --> 01:14:41,331
I can be nutty, just like the rest of you

1909
01:14:41,331 --> 01:14:43,805
