1910
01:14:43,805 --> 01:14:45,787
There's no reason why I can't.

1911
01:14:45,787 --> 01:14:49,954
You know, I'm weird and
that results in creativity.

1912
01:14:50,792 --> 01:14:52,903
Well, speaking of the nutty.

1913
01:14:52,903 --> 01:14:55,942
Here's a word from our
friends at Shake-A-Pudding.

1914
01:14:55,942 --> 01:14:58,525
(upbeat music)

1915
01:15:03,965 --> 01:15:07,902
- [Crow] That was a pretty
good idea, actually.

1916
01:15:07,902 --> 01:15:10,008
- [Joel] Oh, and Sinatra's
going right for the scotch.

1917
01:15:10,008 --> 01:15:12,547
- [Tom] Yeah, wouldn't ya know it.

1918
01:15:12,547 --> 01:15:15,630
Hey, she's got Judy Carne hair there.

1919
01:15:19,032 --> 01:15:20,205
Aah.
(gulps)

1920
01:15:20,205 --> 01:15:21,208
- Mary!
- [Crow] Tyler!

1921
01:15:21,208 --> 01:15:22,458
- [Joel] Moore?

1922
01:15:27,064 --> 01:15:28,525
- [Crow] Put it in the box.

1923
01:15:28,525 --> 01:15:30,179
- [Tom] It's okay.

1924
01:15:30,179 --> 01:15:31,747
Oh, it's a rock tumbler, this should

1925
01:15:31,747 --> 01:15:33,944
pad out the film a little.
- [Joel] Oh no.

1926
01:15:33,944 --> 01:15:35,779
- A nice little toy.

1927
01:15:35,779 --> 01:15:37,720
Portable syncraton unit.

1928
01:15:37,720 --> 01:15:39,725
- [Joel] Oh, you made that up!

1929
01:15:39,725 --> 01:15:43,520
- Dr. Takibana changes
water to ice instantly.

1930
01:15:43,520 --> 01:15:45,921
By accelerating their molecules.

1931
01:15:45,921 --> 01:15:48,396
- [Tom] You accelerate
my molecules, Doctor.

1932
01:15:48,396 --> 01:15:50,679
- Anyone has the power to alter

1933
01:15:50,679 --> 01:15:52,513
molecular structure anywhere.

1934
01:15:52,513 --> 01:15:54,764
- [Crow] And they usually do.
- [Mary] I see.

1935
01:15:54,764 --> 01:15:56,724
Then you can even make ice bullets?

1936
01:15:56,724 --> 01:15:57,557
- Yes!

1937
01:15:59,980 --> 01:16:00,961
(chuckling)

1938
01:16:00,961 --> 01:16:03,628
- [Joel] You think that's funny?

1939
01:16:05,943 --> 01:16:07,020
- [Crow] It's Fritz!

1940
01:16:07,020 --> 01:16:10,437
You can tell by his blinking pinkie ring.

1941
01:16:13,088 --> 01:16:15,338
(grunting)

1942
01:16:16,355 --> 01:16:18,808
- [Tom] Ooh, take down, two points!

1943
01:16:18,808 --> 01:16:22,115
Oh, reversal, another two points.

1944
01:16:22,115 --> 01:16:23,800
- [Crow] You two want some gum?

1945
01:16:23,800 --> 01:16:25,963
- [Tom] It's a lady Sunbeam.

1946
01:16:25,963 --> 01:16:28,130
(beeping)

1947
01:16:29,594 --> 01:16:30,675
- [Atari] That's Mary's signal.

1948
01:16:30,675 --> 01:16:32,992
Just what I've been waiting for.

1949
01:16:32,992 --> 01:16:34,419
- [Jerry] What do you mean?

1950
01:16:34,419 --> 01:16:35,773
- I assumed Q was clever enough

1951
01:16:35,773 --> 01:16:37,389
to detect if anyone was acting.

1952
01:16:37,389 --> 01:16:38,979
- [Joel] Oh, no danger of that.

1953
01:16:38,979 --> 01:16:40,182
- Mary doesn't know who their agent is.

1954
01:16:40,182 --> 01:16:41,015
- You like living dangerously.

1955
01:16:41,015 --> 01:16:42,947
- Let's go, Doctor.
- [Tom] Let's play doctor!

1956
01:16:42,947 --> 01:16:44,717
(Tom chuckles)

1957
01:16:44,717 --> 01:16:46,884
- [Joel] Anytime, Daddy-o.

1958
01:16:48,598 --> 01:16:52,301
- [Crow] See if you can get Rush Limbaugh.

1959
01:16:52,301 --> 01:16:54,657
Yeah, that's him.
(jazzy music)

1960
01:16:54,657 --> 01:16:56,237
- [Tom] Can't get rid of it.

1961
01:16:56,237 --> 01:16:57,281
Get rid of it!

1962
01:16:57,281 --> 01:16:58,829
Dear god, it's on every station!

1963
01:16:58,829 --> 01:16:59,996
Get rid of it.

1964
01:17:01,621 --> 01:17:02,551
Woah.

1965
01:17:02,551 --> 01:17:05,049
- [Joel] We're on the
wrong side of the street!

1966
01:17:05,049 --> 01:17:06,396
- [Tom] Oh, it's Japan.

1967
01:17:06,396 --> 01:17:07,232
- [Atari] Where'd they go?

1968
01:17:07,232 --> 01:17:09,391
- I'm not sure about Dr. Takibana.

1969
01:17:09,391 --> 01:17:12,133
Roberto tried to stop
Fritz, but he got away.

1970
01:17:12,133 --> 01:17:13,926
He made off with the portable syncraton.

1971
01:17:13,926 --> 01:17:15,217
- Syncraton?
- [Mary] Yes!

1972
01:17:15,217 --> 01:17:16,582
- [Tom] Sounds like a soap opera.

1973
01:17:16,582 --> 01:17:19,249
(phone ringing)

1974
01:17:21,222 --> 01:17:24,173
- [Crow] Folks, it's just a phone.

1975
01:17:24,173 --> 01:17:25,006
Pick it up.

1976
01:17:25,006 --> 01:17:26,643
- [Joel] Hey, come on,
it's my dad from Florida,

1977
01:17:26,643 --> 01:17:28,476
shut up Sven, come on!

1978
01:17:30,184 --> 01:17:31,017
Be cool.

1979
01:17:31,017 --> 01:17:32,840
- [Voiceover] Dr. Fritz?
- Ja.

1980
01:17:32,840 --> 01:17:35,059
- [Voiceover] We'll go ahead as planned.

1981
01:17:35,059 --> 01:17:37,846
The ship is waiting at
the Shibaura Maru dock.

1982
01:17:37,846 --> 01:17:38,796
- [Tom] The sheep?

1983
01:17:38,796 --> 01:17:41,765
There's a sheep waiting for them?

1984
01:17:41,765 --> 01:17:45,014
- [Crow] Jawohl, Mein
Kampf, all that stuff.

1985
01:17:45,014 --> 01:17:46,700
- Q must be trying to help Dr. Takibana

1986
01:17:46,700 --> 01:17:48,161
and his son escape!

1987
01:17:48,161 --> 01:17:50,098
- [Joel] Is that part of the plot?

1988
01:17:50,098 --> 01:17:51,598
- [Tom] Who knows.

1989
01:17:56,681 --> 01:17:59,350
(humming)

1990
01:17:59,350 --> 01:18:01,569
- The man we were waiting for.

1991
01:18:01,569 --> 01:18:04,902
- [Crow] We're just waiting for a table.

1992
01:18:05,921 --> 01:18:07,265
- Well.

1993
01:18:07,265 --> 01:18:10,657
- [Tom] So, just plum ran out
of things to say here, huh?

1994
01:18:10,657 --> 01:18:12,811
- [Perez] Senorita, you're coming with us.

1995
01:18:12,811 --> 01:18:14,156
- [Joel] He asked me, he asked me!

1996
01:18:14,156 --> 01:18:16,323
Today my dreams come true!

1997
01:18:17,548 --> 01:18:21,050
- And make sure that Dr.
Takibana doesn't commit suicide.

1998
01:18:21,050 --> 01:18:24,835
- [Crow] Yeah, he's always pullin' that.

1999
01:18:24,835 --> 01:18:26,061
- Papa.

2000
01:18:26,061 --> 01:18:27,491
- [Tom] Oh good, a familiar face.

2001
01:18:27,491 --> 01:18:28,451
Adam West is back.

2002
01:18:28,451 --> 01:18:32,227
- Don't go away, I'll come right back.

2003
01:18:32,227 --> 01:18:34,371
Please don't you try anything.

2004
01:18:34,371 --> 01:18:36,871
- [Tom] Don't touch that dial.

2005
01:18:38,726 --> 01:18:41,393
(ominous music)

2006
01:18:50,260 --> 01:18:54,048
- [Tom] It's like What's
Up Doc all of the sudden.

2007
01:18:54,048 --> 01:18:58,293
- [Joel] Come on, punch it
Hal, I wanna die with you!

2008
01:18:58,293 --> 01:19:00,002
- [Crow] Oh, Chinese fire drill.

2009
01:19:00,002 --> 01:19:04,085
- [Joel] You mean Japanese.
- [Crow] Right, right.

2010
01:19:05,082 --> 01:19:07,695
- [Tom] Oh, they're gonna make balloons.

2011
01:19:07,695 --> 01:19:09,595
- The ship's down there,
you cover the other side!

2012
01:19:09,595 --> 01:19:10,939
- [Tom] I'll cover the waterfront.

2013
01:19:10,939 --> 01:19:13,106
(humming)

2014
01:19:16,443 --> 01:19:17,989
Who's whooping?

2015
01:19:17,989 --> 01:19:19,535
- Just another few minutes!

2016
01:19:19,535 --> 01:19:21,381
I'm sure Fritz will show up!

2017
01:19:21,381 --> 01:19:22,683
- Yes!

2018
01:19:22,683 --> 01:19:24,538
- Roberto.
- [All] Clemente.

2019
01:19:24,538 --> 01:19:26,309
- It's strange you only mentioned Fritz.

2020
01:19:26,309 --> 01:19:27,142
(gasps)

2021
01:19:27,142 --> 01:19:28,815
You should've said Dr. Takibana and Fritz!

2022
01:19:28,815 --> 01:19:29,898
- [Crow] Doh!

2023
01:19:31,952 --> 01:19:33,936
- It's not true!

2024
01:19:33,936 --> 01:19:36,761
- All right, Mr. Q.
(Crow stammering)

2025
01:19:36,761 --> 01:19:38,884
I think you better start talking.

2026
01:19:38,884 --> 01:19:40,933
- [Tom] I was born in the
house my father built.

2027
01:19:40,933 --> 01:19:43,163
- So if Dr. Takibana isn't a Q agent,

2028
01:19:43,163 --> 01:19:46,947
why did you lead us out here like this?

2029
01:19:46,947 --> 01:19:48,037
- Look!

2030
01:19:48,037 --> 01:19:51,280
- [Joel] I don't believe he fell for that.

2031
01:19:51,280 --> 01:19:53,030
- [Tom] Unbelievable.

2032
01:19:54,245 --> 01:19:56,955
- He was only stalling us to
give them time to get away.

2033
01:19:56,955 --> 01:19:58,853
- They'll kill Katherine!

2034
01:19:58,853 --> 01:20:03,504
(gunshots)
- [Crow] They hate these cans!

2035
01:20:03,504 --> 01:20:07,717
- [Tom] Oh, these Ludlum novels are, huh?

2036
01:20:07,717 --> 01:20:10,384
- All right, get inside come on.

2037
01:20:13,018 --> 01:20:14,018
Mighty Jack.

2038
01:20:15,023 --> 01:20:15,883
Mighty Jack!

2039
01:20:15,883 --> 01:20:16,885
- [Man] The door will only open

2040
01:20:16,885 --> 01:20:20,510
for 11 pre-registered voices.
- [Tom] Oceans 11.

2041
01:20:20,510 --> 01:20:22,497
- I'm not one of them.

2042
01:20:22,497 --> 01:20:23,927
- Bring her here.

2043
01:20:23,927 --> 01:20:25,955
(gasps)

2044
01:20:25,955 --> 01:20:27,872
- [Crow] Try swordfish.

2045
01:20:29,773 --> 01:20:31,864
- [Tom] Well then.

2046
01:20:31,864 --> 01:20:34,168
I'm going to change your sparkplugs.

2047
01:20:34,168 --> 01:20:37,356
Ha ha, that will make her talk.

2048
01:20:37,356 --> 01:20:40,408
- I don't think shooting
me is going to help.

2049
01:20:40,408 --> 01:20:41,965
- You're right.

2050
01:20:41,965 --> 01:20:45,154
But now we'll get a chance to
see how good this gadget is!

2051
01:20:45,154 --> 01:20:49,229
- [Joel] We're going to
make monster bubbles!

2052
01:20:49,229 --> 01:20:51,832
(buzzing)

2053
01:20:51,832 --> 01:20:53,582
- [Crow] Jeannie, no!

2054
01:20:54,648 --> 01:20:57,059
Major Nelson snowed on her.

2055
01:20:57,059 --> 01:20:59,181
- [Tom] There, you see, it
flocks evenly with no mess.

2056
01:20:59,181 --> 01:21:00,344
Have a Christmas tree?

2057
01:21:00,344 --> 01:21:02,094
This'll do the trick.

2058
01:21:04,908 --> 01:21:05,908
Dum dum dum.

2059
01:21:07,341 --> 01:21:10,168
- [Crow] Robert Ludlum will
be back in the Uvula Scenario!

2060
01:21:10,168 --> 01:21:11,981
- Don't shoot her!

2061
01:21:11,981 --> 01:21:13,304
It's no use.

2062
01:21:13,304 --> 01:21:14,552
We're lost.

2063
01:21:14,552 --> 01:21:17,504
Q is too strong, there is
nothing we can do to stop them.

2064
01:21:17,504 --> 01:21:19,597
(laughing)

2065
01:21:19,597 --> 01:21:20,430
Go on!

2066
01:21:21,379 --> 01:21:24,899
- [Joel] Fitting room
number four's open, sir.

2067
01:21:24,899 --> 01:21:27,459
- [Crow] Hey, there's a rule,
one person per fitting room.

2068
01:21:27,459 --> 01:21:29,293
- [Fritz] This is quite
an installation here.

2069
01:21:29,293 --> 01:21:33,910
- [Tom] Yes Rick, it is.
(laughing)

2070
01:21:33,910 --> 01:21:35,863
- [Joel] Ah, get me a sandwich, would ya?

2071
01:21:35,863 --> 01:21:37,645
- Can you get to the pier?
- [Tenda] Yes sir!

2072
01:21:37,645 --> 01:21:39,229
- No, I'll go instead.
- [Atari] Hurry!

2073
01:21:39,229 --> 01:21:41,153
- [Joel] Yeah, ham on rye
and take off the anise seed,

2074
01:21:41,153 --> 01:21:42,913
I hate those, okay?

2075
01:21:42,913 --> 01:21:43,841
Thanks.
(splashing)

2076
01:21:43,841 --> 01:21:45,943
- [Tom] Ooh, she's going to the aqua deli.

2077
01:21:45,943 --> 01:21:47,031
(ominous music)

2078
01:21:47,031 --> 01:21:49,772
Scarf Theater will be
back, right after this.

2079
01:21:49,772 --> 01:21:50,605
- Okay.

2080
01:21:54,625 --> 01:21:56,620
- [Crow] It's the Righteous Brothers!

2081
01:21:56,620 --> 01:21:59,137
- [Joel] You've lost that...

2082
01:21:59,137 --> 01:22:00,375
- [Crow] Syncrocylatron.

2083
01:22:00,375 --> 01:22:02,273
- [Joel] Ooh, got a bad clam, huh?

2084
01:22:02,273 --> 01:22:05,190
(muffled groaning)

2085
01:22:09,217 --> 01:22:10,884
Oh not that old gag!

2086
01:22:13,014 --> 01:22:15,514
- [Tom] Dad!
- [Atari] Come on.

2087
01:22:17,205 --> 01:22:18,519
- Move!

2088
01:22:18,519 --> 01:22:20,524
- Go on, no tricks.

2089
01:22:20,524 --> 01:22:23,031
(grunting)

2090
01:22:23,031 --> 01:22:26,444
- [Tom] Ooh, Samsonite luggage.

2091
01:22:26,444 --> 01:22:27,756
- Let's get out of here!

2092
01:22:27,756 --> 01:22:28,589
- Wait.

2093
01:22:30,844 --> 01:22:31,677
Okay.

2094
01:22:31,677 --> 01:22:32,708
- [Crow] Ah, the plot was moving

2095
01:22:32,708 --> 01:22:33,759
a little too fast for his liking.

2096
01:22:33,759 --> 01:22:35,828
(Tom chuckles)

2097
01:22:35,828 --> 01:22:38,828
(suspenseful music)

2098
01:22:41,002 --> 01:22:43,007
- [Tom] Well then.

2099
01:22:43,007 --> 01:22:44,159
- [Joel] It's a pineapple roaster,

2100
01:22:44,159 --> 01:22:46,676
watch us roast your
pineapples slice, you pick it!

2101
01:22:46,676 --> 01:22:48,564
- [Tom] Pineapple roaster?

2102
01:22:48,564 --> 01:22:50,730
- [Crow] I love it.
(laughing)

2103
01:22:50,730 --> 01:22:52,426
- [Joel] That's funny, you gotta admit,

2104
01:22:52,426 --> 01:22:55,426
roasted pineapple slices, it's neat.

2105
01:22:57,923 --> 01:22:59,006
- Okay, come.

2106
01:23:01,844 --> 01:23:02,974
- Hold it!

2107
01:23:02,974 --> 01:23:06,792
- [Tom] Now hold it up to the light.

2108
01:23:06,792 --> 01:23:10,959
Oh that's better, we're in a
completely different film now.

2109
01:23:13,291 --> 01:23:15,103
(humming)

2110
01:23:15,103 --> 01:23:18,603
- [Crow] And we call it the postage meter.

2111
01:23:19,476 --> 01:23:23,092
- We'll surprise them.
- [Perez] Come on!

2112
01:23:23,092 --> 01:23:26,090
Having fun?
- [Crow] Surprise!

2113
01:23:26,090 --> 01:23:29,304
(laughing)
- [Jerry] Down!

2114
01:23:29,304 --> 01:23:31,384
- [Joel] Ah, we shouldn't
have taken the time to laugh!

2115
01:23:31,384 --> 01:23:33,634
(gunshots)

2116
01:23:35,839 --> 01:23:38,172
- [Tom] This thing is great.

2117
01:23:41,807 --> 01:23:43,307
Ooh, a bigger one.

2118
01:23:45,316 --> 01:23:48,233
William Faulkner grabs the package.

2119
01:23:54,721 --> 01:23:55,554
Darn!

2120
01:23:57,402 --> 01:23:58,703
- [Crow] You, stunt left.

2121
01:23:58,703 --> 01:24:01,220
You, slant deep, you,
right sound in the fury.

2122
01:24:01,220 --> 01:24:02,053
Let's go!

2123
01:24:05,668 --> 01:24:08,068
- [Joel] Well, you got holes in your gun!

2124
01:24:08,068 --> 01:24:10,212
- [Crow] Yeah, well you got
peanut butter in my chocolate.

2125
01:24:10,212 --> 01:24:11,212
- [Tom] Hmm?

2126
01:24:14,537 --> 01:24:16,519
- [Crow] Pew Pew.
- [Jerry] Drop it!

2127
01:24:16,519 --> 01:24:18,269
- [Tom] Tadow, tadow!

2128
01:24:22,132 --> 01:24:23,299
- Don't shoot!

2129
01:24:24,482 --> 01:24:26,520
- [Joel] Come on, come on.

2130
01:24:26,520 --> 01:24:28,236
Ooh!
- [Tom] Ooh.

2131
01:24:28,236 --> 01:24:30,039
- [Crow] All right, now you slow dance,

2132
01:24:30,039 --> 01:24:32,291
don't try to lead, I got a gun!

2133
01:24:32,291 --> 01:24:33,208
(Tom chuckles)

2134
01:24:33,208 --> 01:24:35,331
- [Joel] It's the Yancy Street Gang!

2135
01:24:35,331 --> 01:24:37,734
- [Tom] Hasta la vista, baby.
- [Joel] I may be German,

2136
01:24:37,734 --> 01:24:41,083
but I'm fast!
(laughing)

2137
01:24:41,083 --> 01:24:42,833
- [Jerry] Don't move!

2138
01:24:44,317 --> 01:24:47,014
- [Tom] Oh, no way out!

2139
01:24:47,014 --> 01:24:48,455
- [Joel] Hey!
- [Tom] Fritz!

2140
01:24:48,455 --> 01:24:50,321
- [Joel] Come on!
- [Crow] No, don't!

2141
01:24:50,321 --> 01:24:51,688
(explosion)

2142
01:24:51,688 --> 01:24:53,796
- [Tom] Oh, boy.

2143
01:24:53,796 --> 01:24:56,564
- [Crow] He died as he
lived, lovin' his work.

2144
01:24:56,564 --> 01:24:58,456
(Tom chuckles)

2145
01:24:58,456 --> 01:25:01,039
(upbeat music)

2146
01:25:05,240 --> 01:25:07,740
- [Tom] It's Disneyland Tokyo.

2147
01:25:12,097 --> 01:25:15,470
- [Crow] Ah, here we are at plot recovery.

2148
01:25:15,470 --> 01:25:19,270
- All right.
(heavy breathing)

2149
01:25:19,270 --> 01:25:20,364
- [Joel] Everybody get in the shot!

2150
01:25:20,364 --> 01:25:22,018
Come on, stay on camera.
- [Atari] How are you?

2151
01:25:22,018 --> 01:25:23,351
- A little weak.

2152
01:25:24,764 --> 01:25:27,580
Q is going to...
- [Atari] What about Q?

2153
01:25:27,580 --> 01:25:29,713
- They're going to destroy the island.

2154
01:25:29,713 --> 01:25:31,324
In Amori Bay.

2155
01:25:31,324 --> 01:25:33,819
- With the freezing process?
- [Katherine] Yes.

2156
01:25:33,819 --> 01:25:36,050
I overheard Roberto give the order.

2157
01:25:36,050 --> 01:25:38,140
It was for today.

2158
01:25:38,140 --> 01:25:39,698
You must hurry.
- [Tom] Don't touch me.

2159
01:25:39,698 --> 01:25:41,975
Let go of me!
- [Katherine] You must hurry!

2160
01:25:41,975 --> 01:25:44,172
- [Tom] You must sink the Bismark.

2161
01:25:44,172 --> 01:25:46,146
- Get back to Mighty
Jack, full-scale alert.

2162
01:25:46,146 --> 01:25:47,451
- [Mary] Yes sir!
- Combat stations!

2163
01:25:47,451 --> 01:25:48,582
- [All] Yes sir!

2164
01:25:48,582 --> 01:25:51,025
(adventurous music)

2165
01:25:51,025 --> 01:25:53,223
- [Joel] Again with the bank turn!

2166
01:25:53,223 --> 01:25:55,090
- [Tom] Cryin' out loud.
- Increase speed.

2167
01:25:55,090 --> 01:25:56,722
- [Crow] But I'll get carsick!

2168
01:25:56,722 --> 01:25:58,349
- Increase speed.

2169
01:25:58,349 --> 01:26:00,147
- [Atari] Nuclear rockets.

2170
01:26:00,147 --> 01:26:01,480
- Ready to fire.

2171
01:26:02,408 --> 01:26:03,954
- Engine room.

2172
01:26:03,954 --> 01:26:07,411
- Gauge indicates temperatures rising.

2173
01:26:07,411 --> 01:26:09,328
- [Crow] Pineapples up.

2174
01:26:10,311 --> 01:26:11,144
Frost 'em.

2175
01:26:13,073 --> 01:26:14,216
- [Tom] Make 'em icy.

2176
01:26:14,216 --> 01:26:16,925
- Master, ready to engage Mighty Jack!

2177
01:26:16,925 --> 01:26:18,387
- [Tom] Am I still in this film?

2178
01:26:18,387 --> 01:26:20,275
(Crow meows)
- At last.

2179
01:26:20,275 --> 01:26:21,459
- Coolant not reacting?

2180
01:26:21,459 --> 01:26:23,539
Temperature rising.
- [Tom] Mojo rising.

2181
01:26:23,539 --> 01:26:24,956
- Increase speed.

2182
01:26:25,835 --> 01:26:28,247
The iceberg, Q's headquarters.

2183
01:26:28,247 --> 01:26:29,741
- Major, let's hit them right now.

2184
01:26:29,741 --> 01:26:31,491
We'll never have a
better chance than this.

2185
01:26:31,491 --> 01:26:32,749
- [Tom] Yeah.

2186
01:26:32,749 --> 01:26:34,296
- Get ready to fire.
- [Jerry] Right.

2187
01:26:34,296 --> 01:26:37,048
(alarm blaring)
- [Tom] Uh-oh.

2188
01:26:37,048 --> 01:26:39,764
- [Crow] Fries are up.
- What is it?

2189
01:26:39,764 --> 01:26:40,792
What's wrong?

2190
01:26:40,792 --> 01:26:42,086
- [Tom] The A's are much too high, sir!

2191
01:26:42,086 --> 01:26:45,038
- 200, sir, the temperature's
continually rising.

2192
01:26:45,038 --> 01:26:47,960
Another 100 degrees and the
engine room will explode.

2193
01:26:47,960 --> 01:26:49,090
- What are we gonna do?

2194
01:26:49,090 --> 01:26:50,872
- [Joel] Well, don't
go in the engine room.

2195
01:26:50,872 --> 01:26:53,453
- We've got to find a way
to reduce the temperature.

2196
01:26:53,453 --> 01:26:54,888
Jerry!
- [Tom] What, oh, why bother.

2197
01:26:54,888 --> 01:26:56,595
- See if Dr. Takibana can help us, go on!

2198
01:26:56,595 --> 01:26:57,428
- Yes sir!

2199
01:27:04,358 --> 01:27:05,675
- Jerry.

2200
01:27:05,675 --> 01:27:08,324
They better hurry or Q will
blast us right out of here!

2201
01:27:08,324 --> 01:27:10,279
- [Jerry] They're working
on the syncraton now.

2202
01:27:10,279 --> 01:27:13,696
- [Tom] They bought that syncraton thing.

2203
01:27:14,941 --> 01:27:16,978
High school shop classes
are quickly taken.

2204
01:27:16,978 --> 01:27:18,215
- Can't you hurry?

2205
01:27:18,215 --> 01:27:19,888
They're helpless out there!

2206
01:27:19,888 --> 01:27:21,874
- I'm doing all I can.

2207
01:27:21,874 --> 01:27:23,453
Try that switch.
- [Crow] You try it.

2208
01:27:23,453 --> 01:27:24,925
I'm bitter.

2209
01:27:24,925 --> 01:27:28,076
- I'll take over, try the backup system.

2210
01:27:28,076 --> 01:27:31,798
- [Joel] You guys had all
semester to work on this.

2211
01:27:31,798 --> 01:27:34,881
- Yuri, Yuri, how's it going?

2212
01:27:34,881 --> 01:27:36,086
- The temperature's still rising,

2213
01:27:36,086 --> 01:27:38,900
I can't seem to control it.

2214
01:27:38,900 --> 01:27:41,068
- Hurry Doctor, you've
gotta get it working!

2215
01:27:41,068 --> 01:27:42,732
- [Crow] Um, um.

2216
01:27:42,732 --> 01:27:44,705
- Sir, the temperature's still rising.

2217
01:27:44,705 --> 01:27:47,745
We'll explode any second,
what should we do?

2218
01:27:47,745 --> 01:27:50,433
- [Crow] I can't change the
laws of physics, Captain!

2219
01:27:50,433 --> 01:27:52,465
I've got to have 30 minutes!

2220
01:27:52,465 --> 01:27:55,475
- I've got it, it's working now!

2221
01:27:55,475 --> 01:27:56,642
- [Crow] He just plugged it in.

2222
01:27:56,642 --> 01:27:58,626
- It's working, it's working!

2223
01:27:58,626 --> 01:28:00,101
- Direct it onto the engines.

2224
01:28:00,101 --> 01:28:04,061
- [Joel] And get a little
on the plot, if you can.

2225
01:28:04,061 --> 01:28:04,894
- Right.

2226
01:28:04,894 --> 01:28:06,917
- [Crow] You die, Bazooka Joe!

2227
01:28:06,917 --> 01:28:09,230
- All right, now fire.

2228
01:28:09,230 --> 01:28:11,397
(moaning)

2229
